      "body": "Good morning Stella, Just wanted to get back to you on this. These were very helpful. We were able to link our Stockfish 18 Puzzle Miner app to Chessnut Move and Chessnut Go boards. Quite amazing how well it works! We will post the videos to our channel soon. Thanks again for this. Kind Regards, Cyrus On 7/9/2026 4:28 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: > Hi Cyrus, > > Thanks for your interest in integrating with Chessnut boards. > Here are two documentation links that should be helpful for your > development: > Chessnut eBoards API (for Air, Air+, Go, Pro): > https://github.com/chessnutech/Chessnut_eBoards > This covers Bluetooth connection, FEN data retrieval, LED control, and > battery reading for our non-Move boards. > Chessnut Move API (for the Move board): > https://github.com/chessnutech/chess_move_api > This includes everything from the eBoards API, plus additional > features specific to the Move board, such as setting FEN for auto-move > functionality, reading piece status, and more detailed LED color control. > Both repositories are public and contain code examples to help you get > started. Let us know if you have any questions during development! > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > > > ------------------------------------------------------------------ > 发件人：Gadgetify > 发送时间：2026年7月7日(周二) 22:10 > 收件人：Stella Zhuang > 主 题：Re: 回复：Chessnut July Updates – Sale, Companion & New App > > Thank you Stella! Right now, we are working on a comprehensive app > that runs Stockfish 24/7 to find / come up with never seen before > puzzles and studies. We have worked very hard on it, but we would > love to be able to interface it with Chessnut and other boards! > Any documentation that could help us is very much appreciated! > > Best, > > Cyrus > > Gadgetify > > On 7/7/2026 5:11 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: > Hi Cyrus, > > Thanks for your message — glad to hear you’re excited about the > Companion. > We can definitely add you to the list and send one over once we > have stock available. I’ll let you know as soon as it’s ready to ship. > As for the custom app development question — I’ll check with our > tech team and get back to you on that. > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > > > ------------------------------------------------------------------ > 发件人：Gadgetify > 发送时间：2026年7月1日(周三) 06:03 > 收件人：Stella Zhuang > 主 题：Re: Chessnut July Updates – Sale, Companion & New App > > Hi Stella, > > Great update. We would love to test the Chessnut Companion if it > is possible. I think we won a prize from you for being one of the > most active Chessnut posters? If you need tons of videos for the > Chessnut Companion, we can certainly deliver on that. I think it > would go great with the Chessnut Move. We have done reviews of > DGT Pi in the past but this looks 100x times better. Very > exciting! One question: is it codable? Can we develop custom apps > for it? > > Kind Regards, > > Cyrus > > Gadgetify > > On 6/30/2026 5:39 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: > Hi everyone, > > Long time no see — a few quick updates: > > 1. 6th Anniversary Sale (July 1–11) > 20% off storewide — your discount codes work too. We’ve been > running fewer discounts this year, so this is a good one to plan > content around. Good for board reviews, accessories, or anything > you want to feature. If you need us to boost anything, just send > the link. > > 2. Chessnut Companion Launch – July 3, 8:00 AM EST > First batch: 200 units at 20% off → $367.20. > Key features: > - AI coaching & real-time guidance > - Tournament-grade chess clock > - Voice control > - Works with Chess.com, Lichess, and more > - Motorized auto-switch > Compatible with all Chessnut boards except Evo. Only 200 units > available at this price, so it’s worth acting early. Interested? > Submit your content ideas — we’ll review them. > > 3. Chessnut Next – App Overhaul > We’re rolling out a completely redesigned app that turns the > Chessnut board into a full training ecosystem: > - Daily Task & Career mode — Gamified progression with tasks, > points, ELO, bosses, and challenges to keep you engaged every day. > - Maia3 integration — The latest human‑style AI engine helps you > understand why players at different levels tend to make certain > moves, not just what the best move is. > - Multiple analysis reports — Standard / Stockfish, Grandeur, and > Maia3 Human Review — so you can review the same game from three > angles: objective engine, coach-level explanation, and human‑style > insight. > - Progress tools — Mistake Book, themed puzzles, interactive > lessons, and Board Analyzer turn each game review into actionable > practice. > It’s currently in beta. If you’re interested in participating, > just let me know. > > Let me know if you have any questions! > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > > --------------HN0ufKjWM0ai2D8R0LdLFENv Content-Type: multipart/related; boundary=\"------------OqXchgpcvAtaGs3jKE000QN1\" --------------OqXchgpcvAtaGs3jKE000QN1 Content-Type: text/html; charset=UTF-8 Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit Good morning Stella, Just wanted to get back to you on this. These were very helpful. We were able to link our Stockfish 18 Puzzle Miner app to Chessnut Move and Chessnut Go boards. Quite amazing how well it works! We will post the videos to our channel soon. Thanks again for this. Kind Regards, Cyrus On 7/9/2026 4:28 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: Hi Cyrus, Thanks for your interest in integrating with Chessnut boards. Here are two documentation links that should be helpful for your development: Chessnut eBoards API (for Air, Air+, Go, Pro): https://github.com/chessnutech/Chessnut_eBoards This covers Bluetooth connection, FEN data retrieval, LED control, and battery reading for our non-Move boards. Chessnut Move API (for the Move board): https://github.com/chessnutech/chess_move_api This includes everything from the eBoards API, plus additional features specific to the Move board, such as setting FEN for auto-move functionality, reading piece status, and more detailed LED color control. Both repositories are public and contain code examples to help you get started. Let us know if you have any questions during development! Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Gadgetify &lt;gadgetify@gmail.com&gt; 发送时间：2026年7月7日(周二) 22:10 收件人：Stella Zhuang &lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主 题：Re: 回复：Chessnut July Updates – Sale, Companion &amp; New App Thank you Stella! Right now, we are working on a comprehensive app that runs Stockfish 24/7 to find / come up with never seen before puzzles and studies. We have worked very hard on it, but we would love to be able to interface it with Chessnut and other boards! Any documentation that could help us is very much appreciated! Best, Cyrus Gadgetify On 7/7/2026 5:11 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: Hi Cyrus, Thanks for your message — glad to hear you’re excited about the Companion. We can definitely add you to the list and send one over once we have stock available. I’ll let you know as soon as it’s ready to ship. As for the custom app development question — I’ll check with our tech team and get back to you on that. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Gadgetify &lt;gadgetify@gmail.com&gt; 发送时间：2026年7月1日(周三) 06:03 收件人：Stella Zhuang &lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主 题：Re: Chessnut July Updates – Sale, Companion &amp; New App Hi Stella, Great update. We would love to test the Chessnut Companion if it is possible. I think we won a prize from you for being one of the most active Chessnut posters? If you need tons of videos for the Chessnut Companion, we can certainly deliver on that. I think it would go great with the Chessnut Move. We have done reviews of DGT Pi in the past but this looks 100x times better. Very exciting! One question: is it codable? Can we develop custom apps for it? Kind Regards, Cyrus Gadgetify On 6/30/2026 5:39 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: Hi everyone, Long time no see — a few quick updates: 1. 6th Anniversary Sale (July 1–11) 20% off storewide — your discount codes work too. We’ve been running fewer discounts this year, so this is a good one to plan content around. Good for board reviews, accessories, or anything you want to feature. If you need us to boost anything, just send the link. 2. Chessnut Companion Launch – July 3, 8:00 AM EST First batch: 200 units at 20% off → $367.20. Key features: - AI coaching &amp; real-time guidance - Tournament-grade chess clock - Voice control - Works with Chess.com, Lichess, and more - Motorized auto-switch Compatible with all Chessnut boards except Evo. Only 200 units available at this price, so it’s worth acting early. Interested? Submit your content ideas — we’ll review them. 3. Chessnut Next – App Overhaul We’re rolling out a completely redesigned app that turns the Chessnut board into a full training ecosystem: - Daily Task &amp; Career mode — Gamified progression with tasks, points, ELO, bosses, and challenges to keep you engaged every day. - Maia3 integration — The latest human‑style AI engine helps you understand why players at different levels tend to make certain moves, not just what the best move is. - Multiple analysis reports — Standard / Stockfish, Grandeur, and Maia3 Human Review — so you can review the same game from three angles: objective engine, coach-level explanation, and human‑style insight. - Progress tools — Mistake Book, themed puzzles, interactive lessons, and Board Analyzer turn each game review into actionable practice. It’s currently in beta. If you’re interested in participating, just let me know. Let me know if you have any questions! Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut --------------OqXchgpcvAtaGs3jKE000QN1 Content-Type: image/png; name=\"temp4cj.png\" Content-Disposition: inline; filename=\"temp4cj.png\" Content-