      "subject": "Re: Sponsorship Opportunity - Al Ain Chess & Mind Games Club",
      "summary": "Dear Stella, Thank you for the update, and no worries about the delay. The proposed framework sounds great from our side, and I believe it provides a strong fou",
      "body": "Dear Stella, Thank you for the update, and no worries about the delay. The proposed framework sounds great from our side, and I believe it provides a strong foundation for a long-term partnership. We appreciate your openness and look forward to hearing from you once you've discussed the remaining details with your team. Best regards, On Fri, Jul 17, 2026 at 1:27 PM Stella Zhuang wrote: > Hi Ammar, > > Thanks for your follow-up — and sorry for the delay on our side. > This project involves quite a few details, so I'll need to discuss it with > my team before I can give you a clear answer. That said, I'd like to share > my initial thoughts with you, so we can align expectations and move more > efficiently once I come back to you. > Here's what I have in mind: > Products included in the sponsorship: one unit of each product in our > lineup. > Shipping to the UAE: Chessnut will cover the cost of sending the sponsored > units to your location. > Customer purchases: shipping costs for customer orders will be covered by > the buyers themselves. > Partnership duration: we're open to an annual partnership, which would > allow us to support multiple events throughout the year. > Event support: the level of material support will depend on the scale of > each tournament, the number of participants, and the promotional efforts > around it — we'll evaluate case by case. > For the rest, I'll need to discuss internally with my team before I can > confirm anything. > In the meantime, I'd love to hear your thoughts on this framework — > especially if you have any preferences or suggestions on how we could > structure this to work better for both sides. That would help us move > faster once we're ready to finalize. > I'll get back to you as soon as I have a clearer picture. > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > > > ------------------------------------------------------------------ > 发件人：Ammar sbahi > 发送时间：2026年7月15日(周三) 22:01 > 收件人：Stella Zhuang > 主 题：Re: Sponsorship Opportunity - Al Ain Chess & Mind Games Club > > Dear Stella, > > I hope you're doing well. > > I just wanted to follow up on my previous email regarding the potential > partnership between Chessnut and Al Ain Chess Club. > > We remain very interested in exploring this collaboration and would > appreciate any updates regarding the sponsorship details when you have the > opportunity. > > We look forward to hearing from you and hope to move forward together soon. > > Thank you for your time. > > On Wed, Jul 8, 2026 at 12:28 PM Ammar sbahi wrote: > Dear Stella, > > Thank you for your thoughtful proposal and for taking the time to outline > your vision for a long-term partnership. > > We truly appreciate the opportunity and believe this could be the > beginning of a valuable collaboration between Chessnut and Al Ain Chess > Club. > > We are very interested in the product sponsorship model and the pre-order > distribution approach, especially as it allows us to introduce Chessnut > products to our community without the need to hold inventory. > > Before moving forward, we would appreciate a few additional details > regarding: > > - The products included in the sponsorship (models and quantities). > - The estimated annual value of the sponsorship. > - Whether shipping costs to the UAE are covered by Chessnut. > - The distributor margin and ordering process. > - Whether the partnership is intended to be annual and include support > for multiple tournaments and club activities throughout the year. > > Once we have these details, we will be pleased to discuss the next steps > and work together to establish a successful long-term partnership. > > We look forward to your response and are excited about the potential > opportunities this partnership can create for both Chessnut and Al Ain > Chess Club. > > Best regards, > > > Ammar Sbahi > Marketing & Events Coordinator > > *Al Ain Chess & Mind Games Club* > > Landline: +971 3 763 3387 > > Mobile: +971 56 