      "body": "Subject: Valdepeñas affiliate setup Hi Stella, Thanks for the clarification. We’d be happy to move forward with both the dedicated Valdepeñas discount code and the separate affiliate account. I have prepared a different email address for the new affiliate account: ginesdura@gmail.com. However, I couldn’t find the option to register a new affiliate account on the website. Could you please send me the correct link or let me know how I should set it up? Could you also confirm whether the Valdepeñas discount code and the affiliate link can be used together, so customers receive the discount while the sales are still tracked for commission? Regarding the wholesale partnership, we are also considering it and see it as a very viable option in the medium term, particularly after assessing the results from Valdepeñas. Best, Ginés El mar, 14 jul 2026 a las 11:20, Stella Zhuang ( ) escribió: > Hi Ginés, > > Thanks for your thoughtful proposal. We really appreciate the effort > you're putting into this. > To be upfront, the European market has been quite challenging for us > lately, and sales have been slower than we'd hope. Given that, a shared > advertising budget isn't something we can commit to right now. > Instead, I'd like to suggest a few practical alternatives. > First, we can set up a dedicated discount code for the Valdepeñas event. > However, please note that this code will not be linked to affiliate > commissions, as the affiliate program runs on a separate system. The > discount itself is doable, but the tracking mechanism is different. > Second, you can create a separate affiliate program just for Valdepeñas. > You'll just need to sign up with a different email address to set this up. > That way, you'll have your own affiliate link and can earn commissions > automatically on sales generated through it. > Third, if you're looking for better margins, we'd recommend considering a > wholesale partnership. That would give you a real profit margin to work > with, and you'd have more flexibility on pricing and promotions. > We also noticed you mentioned your online store with 300 products. While > that's impressive, our current focus is not on expanding into new online > retail channels. We'd prefer to keep things simple and focused. > Let us know if any of these options work for you. We're happy to explore > what makes sense. > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > > ------------------------------------------------------------------ > 发件人：ChessMagis > 发送时间：2026年7月14日(周二) 03:59 > 收件人：Stella Zhuang > 主 题：Re: Valdepeñas 2026 – Chessnut Promotion Opportunity > > Hi Stella, > > > Our main goal is not only to achieve good results during this event, but > also to build a successful collaboration model that we can replicate and > improve together in future tournaments. We see Valdepeñas as an opportunity > to create a real success story and learn what works best for both Chessnut > and ChessMagis. > > https://www.openlosmolinos.es/ > > Some ideas that came to mind are: > A special discount code for the Valdepeñas event, ideally with an improved > commission structure. > A shared advertising budget, with both Chessnut and ChessMagis investing > to maximize the campaign's reach. > Promotion through Chessnut's official channels, if possible. > > On our side, we are investing our own time, resources, showroom space, > content creation and advertising. We have also recently completed our > online store with almost 300 products, so although we will only bring a > selected range to the event, our goal is to drive online sales before, > during and after the tournament. > > https://chessmagis.com/tienda/ > > These are simply our initial ideas. You know your products and marketing > possibilities much better than we do, so if you think there are other ways > we could work together more effectively, we would be delighted to hear your > suggestions. > Looking forward to your thoughts. > > Best regards, > Ginés > www.chessmagis.com > > El mar, 7 jul 2026, 10:10, Stella Zhuang > escribió: > Hi Ginés, > > Thanks for the detailed proposal — it sounds like a well-planned event > with strong potential for Chessnut exposure.Before we discuss further, > could you clarify what kind of support you’re hoping to receive from > Chessnut? > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > > ------------------------------------------------------------------ > 发件人：ChessMagis > 发送时间：2026年6月9日(周二) 20:15 > 收件人：\"stella.zhuang\" > 主 题：Valdepeñas 2026 – Chessnut Promotion Opportunity > > Hi Stella, > > Thank you for your previous reply and for the insights regarding the > affiliate tracking and discount code usage. It was very helpful. > > After reviewing the situation, we have been planning our next major event > and I wanted to share an idea with you. > > On July 17-19 we will be attending the VIII Open los Molinos in Spain. We > were already present at the event last year and had a very positive > experience there. This year we are preparing a more focused promotional > strategy around Chessnut products. > > https://www.openlosmolinos.es/ > > During a previous event in San Vicente, Chessnut boards were present and > generated interest, but a significant part of our resources had to be > dedicated to managing a large physical chess store, books and other > materials. Valdepeñas will be different. > > Our plan is to create a dedicated Chessnut showroom experience where > players can see, test and interact with the boards throughout the event. We > currently own several Chessnut boards and intend to use them extensively > during the tournament. > > In addition, the boards themselves will become part of the content we > create. We plan to generate content before, during and after the event, > including demonstrations, player interviews, product showcases and social > media coverage. Many of these activities will be conducted directly using > the Chessnut boards. > > We are also considering investing our own resources in promoting this > campaign through content creation and paid advertising in order to maximize > its reach and impact. > > Given this opportunity, we would love to explore whether Chessnut would be > interested in collaborating in any way that could help maximize the results > for both sides. We would be very interested in hearing your thoughts and > learning what types of collaboration opportunities might be available. > > Looking forward to hearing from you. > > Best regards, > > Ginés Durá > www.chessmagis.com > > Subject: Valdepeñas affiliate setup Hi Stella, Thanks for the clarification. We’d be happy to move forward with both the dedicated Valdepeñas discount code and the separate affiliate account. I have prepared a different email address for the new affiliate account: ginesdura@gmail.com . However, I couldn’t find the option to register a new affiliate account on the website. Could you please send me the correct link or let me know how I should set it up? Could you also confirm whether the Valdepeñas discount code and the affiliate link can be used together, so customers receive the discount while the sales are still tracked for commission? Regarding the wholesale partnership, we are also considering it and see it as a very viable option in the medium term, particularly after assessing the results from Valdepeñas. Best, Ginés El mar, 14 jul 2026 a las 11:20, Stella Zhuang (&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt;) escribió: Hi Ginés, Thanks for your thoughtful proposal. We really appreciate the effort you&#39;re putting into this. To be upfront, the European market has been quite challenging for us lately, and sales have been slower than we&#39;d hope. Given that, a shared advertising budget isn&#39;t something we can commit to right now. Instead, I&#39;d like to suggest a few practical alternatives. First, we can set up a dedicated discount code for the Valdepeñas event. However, please note that this code will not be linked to affiliate commissions, as the affiliate program runs on a separate system. The discount itself is doable, but the tracking mechanism is different. Second, you can create a separate affiliate program just for Valdepeñas. You&#39;ll just need to sign up with a different email address to set this up. That way, you&#39;ll have your own affiliate link and can earn commissions automatically on sales generated through it. Third, if you&#39;re looking for better margins, we&#39;d recommend considering a wholesale partnership. That would give you a real profit margin to work with, and you&#39;d have more flexibility on pricing and promotions. We also noticed you mentioned your online store with 300 products. While that&#39;s impressive, our current focus is not on expanding into new online retail channels. We&#39;d prefer to keep things simple and focused. Let us know if any of these options work for you. We&#39;re happy to explore what makes sense. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：ChessMagis &lt; chessmagis@gmail.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年7月14日(周二) 03:59 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主 题：Re: Valdepeñas 2026 – Chessnut Promotion Opportunity Hi Stella, Our main goal is not only to achieve good results during this event, but also to build a successful collaboration model that we can replicate and improve together in future tournaments. We see Valdepeñas as an opportunity to create a real success story and learn what works best for both Chessnut and ChessMagis. https://www.openlosmolinos.es/ Some ideas that came to mind are: A special discount code for the Valdepeñas event, ideally with an improved commission structure. A shared advertising budget, with both Chessnut and ChessMagis investing to maximize the campaign&#39;s reach. Promotion through Chessnut&#39;s official channels, if possible. On our side, we are investing our own time, resources, showroom space, content creation and advertising. We have also recently completed our online store with almost 300 products, so although we will only bring a selected range to the event, our goal is to drive online sales before, during and after the tournament. https://chessmagis.com/tienda/ These are simply our initial ideas. You know your products and marketing possibilities much better than we do, so if you think there are other ways we could work together more effectively, we would be delighted to hear your suggestions. Looking forward to your thoughts. Best regards, Ginés www.chessmagis.com El mar, 7 jul 2026, 10:10, Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; escribió: Hi Ginés, Thanks for the detailed proposal — it sounds like a well-planned event with strong potential for Chessnut exposure.Before we discuss further, could you clarify what kind of support you’re hoping to receive from Chessnut? Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：ChessMagis &lt; chessmagis@gmail.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年6月9日(周二) 20:15 收件人：&quot;stella.zhuang&quot;&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主 题：Valdepeñas 2026 – Chessnut Promotion Opportunity Hi Stella, Thank you for your previous reply and for the insights regarding the affiliate tracking and discount code usage. It was very helpful. After reviewing the situation, we have been planning our next major event and I wanted to share an idea with you. On July 17-19 we will be attending the VIII Open los Molinos in Spain. We were already present at the event last year and had a very positive experience there. This year we are preparing a more focused promotional strategy around Chessnut products. https://www.openlosmolinos.es/ During a previous event in San Vicente, Chessnut boards were present and generated interest, but a significant part of our resources had to be dedicated to managing a large physical chess store, books and other materials. Valdepeñas will be different. Our plan is to create a dedicated Chessnut showroom experience where players can see, test and interact with the boards throughout the event. We currently own several Chessnut boards and intend to use them extensively during the tournament. In addition, the boards themselves will become part of the content we create. We plan to generate content before, during and after the event, including demonstrations, player interviews, product showcases and social media coverage. Many of these activities will be conducted directly using the Chessnut boards. We are also considering investing our own resources in promoting this campaign through content creation and paid advertising in order to maximize its reach and impact. Given this opportunity, we would love to explore whether Chessnut would be interested in collaborating in any way that could help maximize the results for both sides. We would be very interested in hearing your thoughts and learning what types of collaboration opportunities might be available. Looking forward to hearing from you. Best regards, Ginés Durá www.chessmagis.com",
