.com &gt; 主 题：RE: 回复：RE: Relance – Proposition de collaboration 2026 Hi Stella, Thanks for your message! I’m currently based in Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, where I live, so this is a stable address and I’ll be able to receive the package there, even if it ships in May. Here are my shipping details: Joachim Mouhamad Calle Galileo 42, 3º Izquierda A 35010 Las Palmas de Gran Canaria Spain +33 7 76 96 31 25 Please let me know if you need anything else on your side. Best, Joachim De : Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; Envoyé : mercredi 22 avril 2026 12:19 À : Joachim Mouhamad &lt; partenariats.joachimmouhamad@outlook.com &gt; Objet : 回复：RE: Relance – Proposition de collaboration 2026 Hi Joachim, How long will you be staying there? Just so you know, the Move is currently out of stock and may not ship until May. If possible, it would be better to provide a permanent address where you&#39;ll be available to receive the package. Best, Stella ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Joachim Mouhamad &lt; partenariats.joachimmouhamad@outlook.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年4月16日(周四) 21:04 收件人：contact&lt; contact@chessnutech.com &gt; 抄 送：&quot; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &quot;&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主 题：RE: RE: Relance – Proposition de collaboration 2026 Hi Stella, Thanks, it went well — already heading to the next one in France. Thanks for your message — really appreciate it, and the Chessmind feature sounds very interesting from a training perspective. I’d go with the wooden version , as it’s the closest to real tournament conditions. Sounds good to align on starting with a product test first. For shipping, I’m currently based in Las Palmas — happy to share full details if that works on your side. Best, Joachim De : contact &lt; contact@chessnutech.com &gt; Envoyé : mercredi 15 avril 2026 12:42 À : partenariats.joachimmouhamad@outlook.com &lt; partenariats.joachimmouhamad@outlook.com &gt; Cc : stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; Objet : Re: RE: Relance – Proposition de collaboration 2026 ​Hi Joachim, Thanks for your thoughtful reply — and no worries about the delay. Hope the tournament went well! I really agree with your point. Playing against engines and bots is a big part of preparation, and that&#39;s actually where Chessnut fits in perfectly. Our Chessmind feature lets you capture your opponents&#39; games and generate AI that matches their style and level, so you can train against specific types of play very effectively. That said, I fully support starting with a product test — seeing how it naturally fits into your daily training rather than jumping straight into commercial content. That&#39;s exactly what I would prefer as well. Regarding the Chessnut Move, would you prefer the wooden or plastic piece version? In terms of collaboration, our typical model is long‑term: creators produce content, Chessnut handles ad placement, and we also offer an affiliate program (2% extra discount + 5% commission). That&#39;s the baseline. If we find that Chessnut is a great fit for your channel, we&#39;re definitely open to discussing more flexible arrangements. One more thing — I&#39;ve recently migrated my email account. Going forward, please use my new email: stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com . I&#39;ve cc&#39;d this email as well. Looking forward to hearing your thoughts. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut On Mon, 13 Apr at 7:11 PM , Joachim Mouhamad &lt; partenariats.joachimmouhamad@outlook.com &gt; wrote: Hi Stella, Thanks for your patience — I was recently playing a tournament in Las Palmas and just got back to a more normal schedule. After looking into your products more carefully, I believe the most natural integration for me is through the training and preparation phase of my Road to GM journey. A big part of my preparation involves playing against engines and bots. Until now, I was often playing on my phone while manually reproducing the moves on a physical board to stay closer to real tournament conditions — which is not very practical. This is where I see strong value in Chessnut — and more specifically in the Chessnut Move (it feels like the best fit for my use compared to the Pro I initially had in mind) . Being able to train on a real board, with moves played automatically, while staying fully immersed in tournament-like conditions is, in my view, extremely valuable for players who are serious about improving. From a content perspective , I see a natural integration within: My Road To GM tournament videos : (for example, first minutes of this video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AAZ1-9_FZfo ) As well as my tournament preparation storytelling / vlog-style content (for example first minutes of this video : https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OPKQNvDHc48 ) As a starting point, I’d like to test the product and integrate it into my own training. From there, we can define together the most relevant content approach. If this direction makes sense on your side, I’d be happy to explore a structured collaboration. I’d also be interested to understand how you usually structure your partnerships (budget, formats, long-term collaborations, etc.). Best, Joachim De : contact &lt; contact@chessnutech.com &gt; Envoyé : mardi 31 mars 2026 09:33 À : partenariats.joachimmouhamad@outlook.com &lt; partenariats.joachimmouhamad@outlook.com &gt; Objet : Re: RE: Relance – Proposition de collaboration 2026 ​Hi Joachim, Thank you for your detailed message and for sharing your media kit — I&#39;ve reviewed it, and everything looks great. I really appreciate your thoughtful approach. Regarding the Chessnut Pro: we&#39;d be happy to provide one for you. However, I&#39;m afraid it would have to be the standard version (not the premium pieces). I hope you understand — premium pieces are typically not included in influencer collaborations. Thank you for your understanding on this. Now, I have one question about your content style. I noticed that your channel focuses mainly on in-person / over-the-board challenges. Since Chessnut is an electronic board — and one of its key selling points is that you can play without being face to face — how do you plan to integrate Chessnut into your content? I&#39;d love to hear your thoughts on how you would showcase its unique features within your current format. Looking forward to your ideas. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut On Sat, 28 Mar at 4:33 PM , Joachim Mouhamad &lt; partenariats.joachimmouhamad@outlook.com &gt; wrote: Hi Stella, Thanks a lot for your message — no worries at all, and great to connect with you! I really appreciate your feedback on my content, and I agree, I think there’s a strong natural fit between Chessnut and my audience, especially with the Road to GM series and the focus on training, improvement, and performance. I’d definitely be very interested in exploring a long-term collaboration with Chessnut. I’ve attached my media kit so you can have a clearer overview of my audience and current reach. Before going further, I’d love to understand how you usually structure collaborations with creators. Also, is there a specific product you’d like to focus on or push at the moment? From my side, I’m particularly interested in the Chessnut Pro, as it’s the closest to real tournament conditions and would fit perfectly with the content I create. If I were to buy one myself, I would probably go for the version with premium pieces. That said, if it makes sense on your side, I’d also be happy to test and showcase different models to give my audience a clear comparison depending on their budget. To create high-quality and authentic content, I’d love to test one of your boards myself before filming, so I can integrate it naturally into my training and give honest feedback to my audience. For logistics, I’m currently based in Las Palmas de Gran Canaria — please let me know if shipping there would be possible. Looking forward to your thoughts and to building something together. Best, Joachim De : contact &lt; contact@chessnutech.com &gt; Envoyé : vendredi 27 mars 2026 10:39 À : partenariats.joachimmouhamad@outlook.com &lt; partenariats.joachimmouhamad@outlook.com &gt; Objet : Re: Relance – Proposition de collaboration 2026 ​Hi Joachim, Apologies for the delayed reply, I’ve been quite busy with a large event recently. It’s great to connect with you. I’m Stella, Business Development Manager at Chessnut. I’ve taken a look at your channels and really like the direction of your content — I think there’s a strong fit for collaboration. Please feel free to share your media kit with me. I’d also be curious to know if you’ve considered a longer-term partnership. Looking forward to hearing from you Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut On Thu, 19 Mar at 10:38 PM , Joachim Mouhamad &lt; partenariats.joachimmouhamad@outlook.com &gt; wrote: Bonjour l’équipe Chessnut, Je me permets de revenir vers vous concernant une éventuelle collaboration en 2026. Comme mentionné précédemment, je développe une série YouTube Road to GM , où je partage ma progression vers le titre de GM, avec une audience très engagée et en pleine croissance. Si vous êtes ouverts à en discuter, je peux vous transmettre mon media kit ainsi que des idées adaptées à Chessnut. Seriez-vous disponibles pour échanger prochainement ? Merci beaucoup pour votre retour, Joachim Mouhamad YouTube : https://www.youtube.com/@JoachimMouhamad Instagram : https://www.instagram.com/joachimmouhamad/ TikTok : https://www.tiktok.com/@joachim.mouhamad 105085:2750839 106565:2750839",
