      "subject": "Chessnut MOVE / Companion App Testing Feedback – Bugs Identified",
      "summary": "Good morning Stella, I have been testing the app and will continue to do so over the coming days. During testing, I encountered the following issues. *08/07/202",
      "body": "Good morning Stella, I have been testing the app and will continue to do so over the coming days. During testing, I encountered the following issues. *08/07/2026 – MAIA Bot Mode (Chessnut Companion + Chessnut MOVE)* I tested MAIA Bot Mode by playing against MAIA 3 using the Chessnut Companion with the Chessnut MOVE. *Issue 1 – Clock does not start correctly* On the first move of the game, neither White's nor Black's timer started correctly. The expected behaviour is for White's clock to remain idle before the first move. Once White makes the opening move, Black's clock should begin as the game has officially started. For this test the clock did not start until after black had made their first move. *Issue 2 – Increasing delay for chessnut MOVE movements* Each MOVE activation became progressively more delayed as the game continued. After I made a move, the Companion would immediately acknowledge the move, update the position, and switch the clock back to my side. However, the physical piece would not begin moving straight away. The delay increased each turn, for example: - Move 1 – No delay - Move 2 – No delay - Move 3 – Approximately 2 seconds - Move 4 – Approximately 3 seconds - Move 5 – Approximately 4 seconds This continued throughout the game. By move 17, there was approximately a 16-second delay between the Companion acknowledging the move and the Chessnut MOVE beginning to move the piece. After completing the game, I pressed *Restart* to begin a new game. The delay carried over into the new game as well. Black's first move took approximately 12 seconds from the time the Companion acknowledged the move and switched the clock back to me before the piece began moving. ------------------------------ *10/07/2026 – Career Mode / MAIA Difficulty (Chessnut PRO + Chessnut Companion)* After updating to the latest version, I tested Career Mode. I noticed that the MAIA difficulty did not appear to increase between games, despite my Career rating increasing. To verify this, I exited Career Mode and entered MAIA Bot Mode, where I manually selected different MAIA ratings. Regardless of the rating selected, including the strongest setting of 2600, the bot continued to play at what appeared to be the lowest difficulty level. I tested this multiple times with different ratings, but the behaviour remained the same. I will continue testing next week. Regards, Wade Good morning Stella, I have been testing the app and will continue to do so over the coming days. During testing, I encountered the following issues. 08/07/2026 – MAIA Bot Mode (Chessnut Companion + Chessnut MOVE) I tested MAIA Bot Mode by playing against MAIA 3 using the Chessnut Companion with the Chessnut MOVE. Issue 1 – Clock does not start correctly On the first move of the game, neither White&#39;s nor Black&#39;s timer started correctly. The expected behaviour is for White&#39;s clock to remain idle before the first move. Once White makes the opening move, Black&#39;s clock should begin as the game has officially started. For this test the clock did not start until after black had made their first move. Issue 2 – Increasing delay for chessnut MOVE movements Each MOVE activation became progressively more delayed as the game continued. After I made a move, the Companion would immediately acknowledge the move, update the position, and switch the clock back to my side. However, the physical piece would not begin moving straight away. The delay increased each turn, for example: Move 1 – No delay Move 2 – No delay Move 3 – Approximately 2 seconds Move 4 – Approximately 3 seconds Move 5 – Approximately 4 seconds This continued throughout the game. By move 17, there was approximately a 16-second delay between the Companion acknowledging the move and the Chessnut MOVE beginning to move the piece. After completing the game, I pressed Restart to begin a new game. The delay carried over into the new game as well. Black&#39;s first move took approximately 12 seconds from 