      "subject": "[Chessnut Support] Business / Partnership - Chessnut Pro",
      "summary": "New support request from Chessnut website: Name: Giorgio Donnoli Email: developer@chesstools.it Order Number: N/A Inquiry Type: Business / Partnership Product: ",
      "body": "New support request from Chessnut website: Name: Giorgio Donnoli Email: developer@chesstools.it Order Number: N/A Inquiry Type: Business / Partnership Product: Chessnut Pro Description: Subject: ChessFlow — a new iOS training app built for Chessnut boards (launching September) Hi Chessnut team, I&#x27;m Giorgio Donnoli, an iOS developer and active tournament chess player from Italy, and I&#x27;ve spent the past year building an app designed from day one around your boards. ChessFlow turns a Chessnut board into an opening repertoire trainer. You play your prep on the real board; the app follows along with LED guidance and records every move on an electronic scoresheet — the same gesture and mindset as a rated tournament game. Under the hood it schedules each line with spaced repetition, and when a training line ends you can play the position out against Stockfish without leaving the board. You can see it here, with real photos of the app running on an Air+: https://www.chesstools.it/chessflow.html ChessFlow launches on the App Store in September 2026, and it will be one of the few third-party training apps that make owning a Chessnut board *more* valuable — every ChessFlow user is a Chessnut customer, and the product page already tells people which boards to buy. Here&#x27;s where you can help. All development so far has been on my own Chessnut Air+. The BLE protocol should make the app work on the Go and the Pro as well, but I won&#x27;t advertise compatibility I haven&#x27;t verified on real hardware — my users will be tournament players, and they notice. Would you be willing to provide one Chessnut Go and one Chessnut Pro as test units? In return I&#x27;ll certify and maintain full compatibility across the range, list the supported boards prominently on the site and App Store page, and link to your store as the place to get them. I&#x27;m also happy to share TestFlight access so your team can try the app before launch, and to send structured feedback on anything I find in the BLE layer along the way. I&#x27;d love to make ChessFlow the training app Chessnut owners recommend to each other. Shipping two boards is the cheapest marketing you&#x27;ll buy this year. Best regards, Giorgio Donnoli ChessTools — https://www.chesstools.it developer@chesstools.it Video Link: https://www.chesstools.it/chessflow.html --- Submitted via Chessnut Contact Form",
      "bodyEnglish": "New support request from Chessnut website: Name: Giorgio Donnoli Email: developer@chesstools.it Order Number: N/A Inquiry Type: Business / Partnership Product: Chessnut Pro Description: Subject: ChessFlow — a new iOS training app built for Chessnut boards (launching September) Hi Chessnut team, I&#x27;m Giorgio Donnoli, an iOS developer and active tournament chess player from Italy, and I&#x27;ve spent the past year building an app designed from day one around your boards. ChessFlow turns a Chessnut board into an opening repertoire trainer. You play your prep on the real board; the app follows along with LED guidance and records every move on an electronic scoresheet — the same gesture and mindset as a rated tournament game. Under the hood it schedules each line with spaced repetition, and when a training line ends you can play the position out against Stockfish without leaving the board. You can see it here, with real photos of the app running on an Air+: https://www.chesstools.it/chessflow.html ChessFlow launches on the App Store in September 2026, and it will be one of the few third-party training apps that make owning a Chessnut board *more* valuable — every ChessFlow user is a Chessnut customer, and the product page already tells people which boards to buy. Here&#x27;s where you can help. All development so far has been on my own Chessnut Air+. The BLE protocol should make the app work on the Go and the Pro as well, but I won&#x27;t advertise compatibility I haven&#x27;t verified on real hardware — my users will be tournament players, and they notice. Would you be willing to provide one Chessnut Go and one Chessnut Pro as test units? In return I&#x27;ll certify and maintain full compatibility across the range, list the supported boards prominently on the site and App Store page, and link to your store as the place to get them. I&#x27;m also happy to share TestFlight access so your team can try the app before launch, and to send structured feedback on anything I find in the BLE layer along the way. I&#x27;d love to make ChessFlow the training app Chessnut owners recommend to each other. Shipping two boards is the cheapest marketing you&#x27;ll buy this year. Best regards, Giorgio Donnoli ChessTools — https://www.chesstools.it developer@chesstools.it Video Link: https://www.chesstools.it/chessflow.html --- Submitted via Chessnut Contact Form",
