      "summary": "Hey Stella! Would you mind describing what content exactly would Chessnut like to see me do on streams? Or is it just play and analyze type of stream? And what ",
      "body": "Hey Stella! Would you mind describing what content exactly would Chessnut like to see me do on streams? Or is it just play and analyze type of stream? And what board would I be using? And it’s 4 streams per month or per 3 month period? Thank you! On Tue, Jul 7, 2026 at 14:58 Stella Zhuang wrote: > Hi Lena, > > We’re open to testing this with a fixed rate of $500 per month for the > first 3 months (covering 4 streams), with the affiliate commission on top. > If things go well, we can revisit the rate afterward. > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > > ------------------------------------------------------------------ > 发件人：Elena Kotrikadze > 发送时间：2026年7月5日(周日) 06:05 > > 收件人：Stella Zhuang > 主 题：Re: Collaboration Invitation – Chessnut × Twitch Creator > > Hi Stella, > > Thanks for the detail, I like the affiliate structure and I’m happy to > have that as part of the deal. > > But I don’t see a fixed fee mentioned for the streams themselves. That’s > the piece that matters most to me, the affiliate commission can sit on top > as a bonus, not replace it. > Could you share what you’re able to offer as a fixed rate for the 4 > streams a month? > > Best, > Lena > > > On Tue, Jun 30, 2026 at 11:09 Stella Zhuang > wrote: > Hi Lena, > > Thanks for your message. We’d love to explore a long‑term partnership with > you. > To be honest, this would be our first fixed collaboration using live > streams as the main format, so we don’t have a set budget yet. We’re open > to discussing what feels fair — probably something modest to start, and we > can adjust as we go. > In terms of content, we’d be looking at around 1 live stream per week > (about 4 streams a month), plus a Chessnut link in your bio (your own > affiliate link, so purchases count toward your commission). You’ll also get > a discount code that’s 2% higher than our site rate, and a tiered > commission starting at 5%, going up to 10% as sales grow. > We already have creators earning over $5,000 a year through our affiliate > program, and the number keeps growing. If the collaboration goes well, we’d > be happy to tag you as an official Chessnut partner on Instagram and > support your streams regularly — not automatic, but something we’d actively > move toward if we see a good fit. > On the Shenzhen office question — yes, our office is there, but live > streaming is still a relatively new area for us, so I don’t have a clear > answer at this stage. Maybe in the future. > We see this as a real partnership, not a one‑off transaction — something > we’d like to build together over time. > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > > ------------------------------------------------------------------ > 发件人：Elena Kotrikadze > 发送时间：2026年6月26日(周五) 19:38 > 收件人：Stella Zhuang > 主 题：Re: Collaboration Invitation – Chessnut × Twitch Creator > > Hey Stella, I appreciate your honesty and I would absolutely prefer a long > term partnership! Let me know what retainer would look like, how many > streams/reels a month you looking for? > > On a separate note, I am relocation to Shenzhen beginning of next year and > I just saw Rachel did a tour of Chessnut’s office there, I was wondering if > there’s any opportunities for creators in China? No worries if not, just > thought I’d ask. > > Looking forward hearing from you, > Lena. > > On Wed, Jun 24, 2026 at 14:57 Stella Zhuang > wrote: > Hi Lena, > > Thanks for your follow-up, and thank you for your interest in Chessnut and > your kind words about our boards! > Just to be upfront, we're more interested in building a longer‑term > partnership rather than a one‑off project. We'd love to explore something > that works on an ongoing basis, like regular integration in your streams or > content, rather than a single sponsored post or video. > If that sounds like something you'd be open to, we'd be happy to discuss > what that could look like. > Let us know your thoughts. We're excited about the possibility of