      "subject": "Re: Chessnut July Updates – Sale, Companion & New App",
      "summary": "Hi Stella, Great update. We would love to test the Chessnut Companion if it is possible. I think we won a prize from you for being one of the most active Chessn",
      "body": "Hi Stella, Great update. We would love to test the Chessnut Companion if it is possible. I think we won a prize from you for being one of the most active Chessnut posters? If you need tons of videos for the Chessnut Companion, we can certainly deliver on that. I think it would go great with the Chessnut Move. We have done reviews of DGT Pi in the past but this looks 100x times better. Very exciting! One question: is it codable? Can we develop custom apps for it? Kind Regards, Cyrus Gadgetify On 6/30/2026 5:39 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: > Hi everyone, > > Long time no see — a few quick updates: > > 1. 6th Anniversary Sale (July 1–11) > 20% off storewide — your discount codes work too. We’ve been running > fewer discounts this year, so this is a good one to plan content > around. Good for board reviews, accessories, or anything you want to > feature. If you need us to boost anything, just send the link. > > 2. Chessnut Companion Launch – July 3, 8:00 AM EST > First batch: 200 units at 20% off → $367.20. > Key features: > - AI coaching & real-time guidance > - Tournament-grade chess clock > - Voice control > - Works with Chess.com, Lichess, and more > - Motorized auto-switch > Compatible with all Chessnut boards except Evo. Only 200 units > available at this price, so it’s worth acting early. Interested? > Submit your content ideas — we’ll review them. > > 3. Chessnut Next – App Overhaul > We’re rolling out a completely redesigned app that turns the Chessnut > board into a full training ecosystem: > - Daily Task & Career mode — Gamified progression with tasks, points, > ELO, bosses, and challenges to keep you engaged every day. > - Maia3 integration — The latest human‑style AI engine helps you > understand why players at different levels tend to make certain moves, > not just what the best move is. > - Multiple analysis reports — Standard / Stockfish, Grandeur, and > Maia3 Human Review — so you can review the same game from three > angles: objective engine, coach-level explanation, and human‑style > insight. > - Progress tools — Mistake Book, themed puzzles, interactive lessons, > and Board Analyzer turn each game review into actionable practice. > It’s currently in beta. If you’re interested in participating, just > let me know. > > Let me know if you have any questions! > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > > --------------YMcxJ9pJSbGnsaUHHsWXmb3K Content-Type: multipart/related; boundary=\"------------RXQ00eFUf2NOxrwWPCMmAH1c\" --------------RXQ00eFUf2NOxrwWPCMmAH1c Content-Type: text/html; charset=UTF-8 Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit Hi Stella, Great update. We would love to test the Chessnut Companion if it is possible. I think we won a prize from you for being one of the most active Chessnut posters? If you need tons of videos for the Chessnut Companion, we can certainly deliver on that. I think it would go great with the Chessnut Move. We have done reviews of DGT Pi in the past but this looks 100x times better. Very exciting! One question: is it codable? Can we develop custom apps for it? Kind Regards, Cyrus Gadgetify On 6/30/2026 5:39 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: Hi everyone, Long time no see — a few quick updates: 1. 6th Anniversary Sale (July 1–11) 20% off storewide — your discount codes work too. We’ve been running fewer discounts this year, so this is a good one to plan content around. Good for board reviews, accessories, or anything you want to feature. If you need us to boost anything, just send the link. 2. Chessnut Companion Launch – July 3, 8:00 AM EST First batch: 200 units at 20% off → $367.20. Key features: - AI coaching &amp; real-time guidance - Tournament-grade chess clock - Voice control - Works with Chess.com, Lichess, and more - Motorized auto-switch Compatible with all Chessnut boards except Evo. Only 200 units available at this price, so it’s worth acting early. Interested? Submit your content ideas — we’ll review them. 3. Chessnut Next – App Overhaul We’re rolling ou