      "bodyEnglish": "Hi Stella, Great update. We would love to test the Chessnut Companion if it is possible. I think we won a prize from you for being one of the most active Chessnut posters? If you need tons of videos for the Chessnut Companion, we can certainly deliver on that. I think it would go great with the Chessnut Move. We have done reviews of DGT Pi in the past but this looks 100x times better. Very exciting! One question: is it codable? Can we develop custom apps for it? Kind Regards, Cyrus Gadgetify On 6/30/2026 5:39 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: > Hi everyone, > > Long time no see — a few quick updates: > > 1. 6th Anniversary Sale (July 1–11) > 20% off storewide — your discount codes work too. We’ve been running > fewer discounts this year, so this is a good one to plan content > around. Good for board reviews, accessories, or anything you want to > feature. If you need us to boost anything, just send the link. > > 2. Chessnut Companion Launch – July 3, 8:00 AM EST > First batch: 200 units at 20% off → $367.20. > Key features: > - AI coaching & real-time guidance > - Tournament-grade chess clock > - Voice control > - Works with Chess.com, Lichess, and more > - Motorized auto-switch > Compatible with all Chessnut boards except Evo. Only 200 units > available at this price, so it’s worth acting early. Interested? > Submit your content ideas — we’ll review them. > > 3. Chessnut Next – App Overhaul > We’re rolling out a completely redesigned app that turns the Chessnut > board into a full training ecosystem: > - Daily Task & Career mode — Gamified progression with tasks, points, > ELO, bosses, and challenges to keep you engaged every day. > - Maia3 integration — The latest human‑style AI engine helps you > understand why players at different levels tend to make certain moves, > not just what the best move is. > - Multiple analysis reports — Standard / Stockfish, Grandeur, and > Maia3 Human Review — so you can review the same game from three > angles: objective engine, coach-level explanation, and human‑style > insight. > - Progress tools — Mistake Book, themed puzzles, interactive lessons, > and Board Analyzer turn each game review into actionable practice. > It’s currently in beta. If you’re interested in participating, just > let me know. > > Let me know if you have any questions! > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > > --------------YMcxJ9pJSbGnsaUHHsWXmb3K Content-Type: multipart/related; boundary=\"------------RXQ00eFUf2NOxrwWPCMmAH1c\" --------------RXQ00eFUf2NOxrwWPCMmAH1c Content-Type: text/html; charset=UTF-8 Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit Hi Stella, Great update. We would love to test the Chessnut Companion if it is possible. I think we won a prize from you for being one of the most active Chessnut posters? If you need tons of videos for the Chessnut Companion, we can certainly deliver on that. I think it would go great with the Chessnut Move. We have done reviews of DGT Pi in the past but this looks 100x times better. Very exciting! One question: is it codable? Can we develop custom apps for it? Kind Regards, Cyrus Gadgetify On 6/30/2026 5:39 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: Hi everyone, Long time no see — a few quick updates: 1. 6th Anniversary Sale (July 1–11) 20% off storewide — your discount codes work too. We’ve been running fewer discounts this year, so this is a good one to plan content around. Good for board reviews, accessories, or anything you want to feature. If you need us to boost anything, just send the link. 2. Chessnut Companion Launch – July 3, 8:00 AM EST First batch: 200 units at 20% off → $367.20. Key features: - AI coaching &amp; real-time guidance - Tournament-grade chess clock - Voice control - Works with Chess.com, Lichess, and more - Motorized auto-switch Compatible with all Chessnut boards except Evo. Only 200 units available at this price, so it’s worth acting early. Interested? Submit your content ideas — we’ll review them. 3. Chessnut Next – App Overhaul We’re rolling out a completely redesigned app that turns the Chessnut board into a full training ecosystem: - Daily Task &amp; Career mode — Gamified progression with tasks, points, ELO, bosses, and challenges to keep you engaged every day. - Maia3 integration — The latest human‑style AI engine helps you understand why players at different levels tend to make certain moves, not just what the best move is. - Multiple analysis reports — Standard / Stockfish, Grandeur, and Maia3 Human Review — so you can review the same game from three angles: objective engine, coach-level explanation, and human‑style insight. - Progress tools — Mistake Book, themed puzzles, interactive lessons, and Board Analyzer turn each game review into actionable practice. It’s currently in beta. If you’re interested in participating, just let me know. Let me know if you have any questions! Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut --------------RXQ00eFUf2NOxrwWPCMmAH1c Content-Type: image/png; name=\"temp4cj.png\" Content-Disposition: inline; filename=\"temp4cj.png\" Content-Id: Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64 iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAApoAAANwCAYAAACPpMqvAAAgAElEQVR4nOydeXRcxZX/v/16 71a31NosWau12bJkW5Ll3XjBGAPGCzH7hEBghi3kJGROMoFMZhJmJnOSyWSGBAayAYGwBDAE zGITg3FsbORdtiRLlmy0WNa+97693x8+t1z93LJFglh+uZ9zdCR1v/eqXlW9qm/de6ueDoAK hmGYzwCdTgdFUaCqKlT1bFekKAqi0aj42263Izc3FwUFBUhLS0N+fj7S0tKQk5ODzMxMJCYm YmxsDG+//TZ+9rOfoa+vD0ajUVwjGo1Cp9OJvxmGYZhPD8NnnQGGYf52IaEZDoeh0+nE/4qi wOVyoaCgADNnzkRVVRWqqqpQUlICq9WKEydOwOFwIDU1FUajEcePH8drr72GoaEhGAwGhEIh 6HQ6GI1GAICqqkJsMgzDMJ8eLDQZhvnMICumwWAQYtDpdCInJwdLlizBxo0bsXDhQpjNZoyM jKCrqwsdHR3YunUrqqursXjxYthsNnR1daGrqwvRaBQ2mw1+vx+qqgrraCQS+YzvlGEY5m8T FpoMw3xmkBXTZDLB7/fD5XJh48aNuP3221FRUYFoNAq3242Ojg688847ePLJJ9HS0gKdToeC ggLYbDa4XC4sWbIEt956K371q1/B5/MhISEBHo8HoVBICE7ZPc8wDMN8eqj8wz/8wz+T9aPX 6+N+riiKajabVavVqur1erWwsFB9+umn1YGBAVVVVTUSiagNDQ3qAw88oGZmZqo6nU61WCxq amqqmpiYqK5cuVJ94okn1K6uLlVVVTUYDKq1tbXqqlWrVIPBoKampqoWi0U1GAwiDzqd7jMv D/7hH/7hn7+lHz2AH4BhGGY