      "summary": "Hi Stella, Thanks for getting back to me. Here is the contact phone number for the shipment: +48 728 141 413 . Just to make sure we are on the same page regardi",
      "body": "Hi Stella, Thanks for getting back to me. Here is the contact phone number for the shipment: +48 728 141 413 . Just to make sure we are on the same page regarding the boards, as we agreed in the previous email: 2 boards are for the players: Chessnut Pro for the 1st place winner and Chessnut Air+ for the raffle/lottery. 1 board is for Marianczello: Chessnut Move will stay with him for his dedicated content and product placement (Reel/Short and organic video mentions). Krzysztof Dettlaff Jastarnia Ul Ogrodowa 35 84-140 Polska Dnia 30 czerwca 2026 10:10 Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; napisał(a): Hi Krzysztof, Thanks for the shipping address. Could you also provide a contact phone number for the shipment? Also, just to confirm — the prizes we discussed are: 1st place: Chessnut Pro, 2nd place: Chessnut Move, and the raffle prize: Chessnut Air+. Let me know if that still matches your plan. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl &lt;krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月30日(周二) 15:52 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主 题：回复：Odp: 回复：Partnership X Marianczello Decade Series Hi, That sounds perfect, I completely agree. Let&#39;s go ahead with this plan. Marianczello will be happy to create a dedicated Short/Reel with the board and include organic mentions in his future videos. Co-tagging on Instagram is also a great idea. Could you please send me the link to the specific product/board model we are talking about? I’d like to check out the details. In the meantime, here are the shipping details for the 3 boards: Krzysztof Dettlaff Ul.Ogrodowa 35 84-140 Jastarnia Polska Let me know if you need anything else to move forward. Best regards, Krzysztof Wystarczy, że uzupełnisz swoje dane adresowe w pogrubionym bloku i możesz wysyłać. Jeśli chcesz, żebym pomógł Ci przygotować coś jeszcze (np. krótki plan na tę rolkę/Shortsa , gdy już dostaniesz link i szachownicę), daj mi znać! Odpowiedzi wygenerowane przez AI mogą zawierać błędy. support.google.com Więcej informacji Dnia 30 czerwca 2026 09:16 Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; napisał(a): Hi Krzysztof, Thanks for the alternative proposal — that’s actually a smart approach. Sending the third board directly to Marianczello makes sense, as it gives him the product on hand for dedicated content, rather than just a one‑off mention. Let’s go with this option: 2 boards for the players (1 for the Grand Prix winner, 1 for the raffle), and 1 board for Marianczello to feature in his content. For the content side, we’d be happy to have the board featured in a dedicated Reel or Short, and of course any organic mentions in his videos are always welcome. We’re also open to co‑tagging on Instagram when the content goes live. Let me know if this works for you, and we can move forward with the shipping details. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl &lt;krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月26日(周五) 15:49 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主 题：回复：Odp: 回复：Partnership X Marianczello Decade Series Alternatively, we could also propose another option for the prize distribution: We could award 2 boards to the players (one for the final Grand Prix winner and one for the raffle), and the 3rd board could be shipped directly to the creator, Marianczello. This way, he will have the product on hand to record dedicated content and reviews about your brand. Please let me know which of these options works best for you! Dnia 26 czerwca 2026 08:32 Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; napisał(a): Hi Krzysztof, Thanks for the detailed response — this is very helpful. On co-created content: I was thinking we could tag each other when posting Shorts or Reels, so Chessnut’s 60K followers can also discover the tournament. I think that could be a nice boost for visibility on your side too. Also, it might be helpful to feature the prize boards briefly in Marianczello’s video — showing the actual products could make them more appealing to players. The Move is quite popular right now, so that could generate some extra interest. Before we confirm the prize commitment, I have a couple of questions: - Are there other brand sponsors involved in the series besides Chessnut? If so, could you share who they are? - How will the 3 Chessnut boards be used across the 10 tournaments? Will they be awarded at the final Grand Prix standings, or distributed across individual events? - If there are other sponsors, will the Chessnut boards be presented as standalone prizes, or grouped together with other sponsor items? Also, could you confirm the timeline for Marianczello’s YouTube videos and mentions? Looking forward to your reply! Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl &lt;krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月25日(周四) 18:36 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主 题：Odp: 回复：Partnership X Marianczello Decade Series Hi Stella, I am the lead organizer and creator of this event, as well as the administrator of the MARIANCZELLO Club on Chess.com Chess.com . Marianczello and I are close friends; he was actually my very first chess coach. This entire cycle is being organized to celebrate his 10th anniversary as a content creator. To answer your questions directly: Role &amp; Structure: I operate independently but with Marianczello&#39;s full backing. This is a non-profit project driven entirely by my passion to popularize chess. There are no entry fees, and I am not making any profit from it. Tournament Format: It is a hybrid Grand Prix system consisting of 10 monthly editions . In each standalone edition, the top 3 players win prizes, and additional sponsor items are raffled among all participants. Concurrently, the top 30 players from each edition earn points toward a general Grand Prix standing. The biggest guaranteed prizes are reserved for the overall Top 6, alongside a separate raffle pool for active club members. Timeline: We kick off this Sunday, June 28 . Each subsequent edition will take place on the last Sunday of every month, concluding with the grand finale in March 2027 . Player Turnout &amp; Registration: The event is officially hosted on the Chess.com Chess.com Events platform. Because of how the platform works, official player registration opens exactly one hour before the tournament starts. However, based on our club&#39;s active community size, we are expecting a very strong turnout. Exposure &amp; Marketing: We have fantastic channels lined up! Chess.com Chess.com Polska has already published information about our tournament and will promote it again right before the launch. Additionally, Marianczello will be live-streaming parts of the tournament cycle (schedule permitting). We are also planning to include dedicated sponsor mentions and product placements directly inside Marianczello’s upcoming YouTube videos. Regarding your mention of co-creating content, could you please provide more details on what exactly you have in mind? Once I have more specifics, I will consult directly with Marianczello to see what formats we can best integrate into his channel. Please let me know if this structure aligns with Chessnut&#39;s goals, and we can discuss how to move forward! Best regards, Krzysztof Lead Organizer | MARIANCZELLO Club Dnia 25 czerwca 2026 12:07 Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; napisał(a): Hi Krzysztof, Thanks for the detailed proposal — it sounds like a well-structured event with strong community backing. Before we move forward, I have a few questions: - Are you part of Marianczello’s team, or an independent organizer working with him? - Could you clarify the structure of the 10-tournament cycle? Is it 10 separate events with their own winners, or a points-based series leading to one overall champion? - Roughly how many players have registered so far? - You mentioned that 3 boards would help ‘create massive buzz across the 10-tournament cycle’ — could you clarify what the exposure channels look like? Are there social media promotions, media coverage, or other content formats? We’d also be open to co-creating content together. This will help us get a clearer picture and move forward more confidently. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl &lt;krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月25日(周四) 15:05 收件人：&#34;stella.zhuang&#34;&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主 题：Partnership X Marianczello Decade Series Dear Stella, Thank you for the quick response! I am very excited about your interest in collaborating. To give you more details about the event: I am the official organizer of the Marianczello Decade Series —a prestigious cycle of 10 tournaments celebrating Marianczello&#39;s 10th anniversary of chess content creation. He is the biggest chess YouTuber in Poland, with a community of over 150,000 subscribers and 50,000 members in our Chess.com Chess.com club. Initially, I mentioned a single board, but after finalizing the tournament structure, we would love to upgrade this to a partnership involving 3 Chessnut boards . This will allow us to create a massive buzz and maximize the marketing value for Chessnut across the entire 10-tournament cycle: 1st Board: The ultimate Grand Prix prize for the overall winner of the Decade Series. 2nd Board: The prize for the runner-up (2nd place) in the final standings. 3rd Board: A grand raffle prize for all participants. At the end of the series, we will host a big giveaway drawing from everyone who played, which is the perfect tool to keep everyday amateur players highly engaged and active from the first to the very last tournament. In exchange for these 3 boards, we will provide an extensive promotional campaign: Club Homepage Banner: A prominent Chessnut banner on our main Chess.com Chess.com club page for the entire duration of the series. Dedicated Articles &amp; Newsletters: Official tournament announcements on Chess.com Chess.com with direct links to your store, sent to our 50,000 club members. YouTube Video Integration: Marianczello will personally provide dedicated sponsor shoutouts, mention your brand in his videos, and include direct links in the descriptions of his tournament coverage videos on YouTube. This setup ensures high, long-term player engagement and puts Chessnut products directly in front of thousands of passionate Polish chess players for months. Please let me know if this expanded package works for you! Best regards, Krzysztof Dettlaff Tournament Organizer www.chess.com https://www.chess.com/events/info/marianczello-decade-series m.youtube.com https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=41iJsK6L7mI 1:20 Last video and Youtuber talk about tournament and sponsors :) --2MGMPTSVENPBLQFCXNWFRnhgwp Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable Content-Type: text/html; charset=UTF-8 Hi Stella, Thanks for getting back to me. Here is the contact phone number for the shipment: +48 728 141 413 . Just to make sure we are on the same page regarding the boards, as we agreed in the previous email: 2 boards are for the players: Chessnut Pro for the 1st place winner and Chessnut Air+ for the raffle/lottery. 1 board is for Marianczello: Chessnut Move will stay with him for his dedicated content and product placement (Reel/Short and organic video mentions). Krzysztof Dettlaff Jastarnia Ul Ogrodowa 35 84-140 Polska Dnia 30 czerwca 2026 10:10 Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; napisał(a): Hi Krzysztof, Thanks for the shipping address. Could you also provide a contact phone number for the shipment? Also, just to confirm — the prizes we discussed are: 1st place: Chessnut