or the hotel, could > already make it feasible for me to attend. > > And if it's not possible, please let me know as well so I can look for > another solution and plan accordingly. > > Best, Tim > > Hi Stella, Thank you so much for your kind and motivating message. It really means a lot to me, and I&#39;m very happy to hear that you&#39;ve been following my progress closely! I am really happy with how the Tiktok and Instagram accounts are growing. No worries at all regarding the tournament sponsorship. I just wanted to be sure so that I could plan accordingly. Regarding the agreement, yes, I can definitely commit to at least one piece of content per day during the summer break. There may be a few rare occasions where I can&#39;t post because of an important emergency, but overall I&#39;m happy with this goal. In fact, knowing that there are people supporting me and following my journey also helps me stay consistent. I can also confirm that the address and all the information are correct. Thank you again! I&#39;m really looking forward to trying the chess clock. If I make a video about it, should I send you the link so you can promote it as before? Also can you explain to me how I can do a collaboration post with Chessnut on instagram like you did with Swapnil, Rachel, etc? I would like to do more posts like this to reach more people showcasing the boards but I&#39;m not sure how to do it. And I&#39;m not sure if you saw my WhatsApp message, but I was wondering if it would be possible to get access to the photos from the tournament—both the pictures of us with the Chessnut boards and the photos taken during the games. I&#39;d love to use some of them for profile pictures and social media posts. I also wanted to ask if you happen to have a more basic Chessnut T-shirt available, maybe with just a small logo on it. If so, I&#39;d love one! Thank you again for all your support! Best, Tim Le mar. 30 juin 2026 à 08:05, Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 