      "summary": "Hi Alan, Thank you very much for your reply, for taking the time to answer my questions, and for sharing the distributor price list along with the additional in",
      "body": "Hi Alan, Thank you very much for your reply, for taking the time to answer my questions, and for sharing the distributor price list along with the additional information. Regarding your comment, no offense taken at all. On the contrary, I completely understand your point of view. I have identified that this category could have significant potential in Mexico. That is precisely why I have decided to approach this project in a structured way. The information you shared will be an important part of my analysis, and I will complement it by validating the opportunity within the Mexican market. My objective is to ensure that every decision regarding this project is supported by real data rather than by an initial perception alone. I already have a specialized project defined, focused exclusively on smart chess. Its objective is to build a dedicated presence around this category, create valuable content, and measure the real response of the Mexican market. At the same time, I will also work on the logistics and import aspects to ensure that, if the project confirms the potential I have identified, it can be developed in a serious, professional, and sustainable way. Chess has been a personal passion of mine for many years, and for that reason I don't see this as a short-term opportunity, but as something I want to build with a long-term vision. I hope to get back in touch once I have meaningful progress to share. I look forward to showing you how the project evolves and continuing our conversation. Thank you again for your time, your openness, and all the information you have shared. Kind regards, David El Mon, Jun 29, 2026 a las 1:37 AM, alan.wang@chessnutech.com &lt;alan.wang@chessnutech.com&gt; escribió: hi David, no offense but it is quite a new area for you. some short answer/bkg for your reference 1. cert we cert FCC/CE which allowes us to sell in US/EU HS code: 9504903000 2. build price: see attached price list 3. logisic we do FOB china city and no consignee shipping mode accepted. you need logistic agent to cover. 4. warranty one year. br Alan alan.wang@chessnutech.com &nbsp; 发件人： &nbsp; david@popokani.mx 发送时间： &nbsp;2026-06-25&nbsp;20:48 收件人： &nbsp; alan.wang@chessnutech.com 抄送： &nbsp; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com 主题： &nbsp;Re: Re：[Chessnut Support] Business / Partnership - Chessnut Move Hello Alan, Thank you for your reply. Yes, you have reached the correct company. I am the founder of Popokani, a Mexican company focused on importing and distributing specialized products. Our current business is primarily related to the RAW brand and its accessories, which is why that is the main focus shown on our website. However, for some time we have been evaluating the possibility of developing a new business category focused on specialized technology products, and Chessnut is one of the brands that has attracted our attention the most. In addition to my experience in international trade and import operations, I have been a chess enthusiast for many years and I understand the growing interest in smart chess products within the chess community. We have a structured process for evaluating new product categories before incorporating them into our portfolio. Our goal is to understand the entire value chain, from importation and regulatory compliance to commercialization and final customer sales. For this reason, we are requesting detailed technical and commercial information. Before evaluating distribution or sales strategies, we need to fully understand logistics, import requirements, technical documentation, transportation costs, and regulatory considerations. Since these are electronic products, we understand that the process is very different from simpler product categories, and we want to make sure everything is handled properly from the beginning. We are not looking to approach this as an improvised project. Our interest is to understand the category professionally and determine whether we can build a solid and sustainable operation around the Chessnut product line in Mexico. I also apologize for the number of questions. Our intention is simply to understand all legal, logistical, and commercial requirements before moving forward, ensuring that any future operation is carried out efficiently and in full compliance with Mexican regulations. Thank you again for your time and willingness to answer our questions. I look forward to receiving any additional information you can share regarding the Chessnut product line and distribution program. Best regards, David Mitchel Rios Bernal Founder – Popokani david@popokani.mx On Wed, Jun 24, 2026 at 7:03 PM alan.wang@chessnutech.com &lt;alan.wang@chessnutech.com&gt; wrote: hello Sir, thanks for your mail. and may I know your biz coveraget as well. from your website seems you focus on tabacco rather than electronic device. maybe I didnt reach the correct web site? br Alan alan.wang@chessnutech.com &nbsp; 发件人： &nbsp; david@popokani.mx 发送时间： &nbsp;2026-06-25&nbsp;08:31 收件人： &nbsp; alan.wang@chessnutech.com 抄送： &nbsp; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com 主题： &nbsp;Re: 回复：[Chessnut Support] Business / Partnership - Chessnut Move Hello Alan, Thank you very much for your response and for the information you have shared so far. We are interested in continuing our evaluation of Chessnut Move from a commercial, logistics and regulatory perspective in order to properly understand the product's viability in the Mexican market. Before moving forward with any future planning, would it be possible to share the following information? Product Complete technical datasheet for Chessnut Move. Available certifications (FCC, CE, RoHS, etc.). HS Code currently used for export. Commercial Current distributor price for Chessnut Move. Complete Chessnut product catalog. Distributor price list for the full product range. MOQ for future reorder purchases. Current stock availability. Logistics Incoterm normally used for international distributors. Shipping origin city in China. Whether Chessnut normally arranges international transportation for distributors or if distributors typically manage logistics independently. Whether you regularly work with FedEx for international shipments. Whether shipments can be arranged using the customer's FedEx account. Documentation Documentation normally provided for export shipments (Commercial Invoice, Packing List, certificates, declarations, or any other relevant documentation). Warranty &amp; Support Warranty policy for international distributors. Standard procedure for handling warranty claims, replacements, or defective products. We apologize for the number of questions. As part of our evaluation process, we need to fully understand the technical, logistics, regulatory and compliance requirements involved in importing and distributing the product in Mexico. Our goal is to ensure that any future operation is carried out efficiently, professionally and fully within the applicable legal and regulatory framework. Thank you again for your support. We look forward to hearing from you. Best regards, David Mitchel Rios Bernal Popokani México&nbsp; On Wed, Jun 24, 2026 at 2:11 AM alan.wang@chessnutech.com &lt;alan.wang@chessnutech.com&gt; wrote: hello Mr. David, nice to know you show interest in distribute Chessnut in Mexico, currenlty Mexico is open for new disti partner.&nbsp; back to your Q&amp;A * Distributor / reseller programs * Wholesale pricing A: yes, usually 40% discount to disti partner * Minimum order quantities (MOQ) A: 5000$ per order and with one time sample order exception during beginning stage. * Sample purchase options A: you can buy from U.S as we run webstore/AMZ in us * Current distribution status in Mexico A: one partnernow * Whether Mexico currently has an exclusive distributor A: No. also please be aware of folloiwng condition: 1. we do FOB china, you need to be capable to import from China or by you logistic partner. 2. the VAT % is quite heavy for Mexico import from China, please double check. thanks br Alan&nbsp; alan.wang@chessnutech.com &nbsp; 发件人： &nbsp; Stella Zhuang 发送时间： &nbsp;2026-06-24&nbsp;16:05 收件人： &nbsp; david ; Alan Wang 主题： &nbsp;回复：[Chessnut Support] Business / Partnership - Chessnut Move Hi Alan, please take a look at this email. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：contact &lt;contact@chessnutech.com&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月24日(周三) 12:26 收件人：\"stella.zhuang\"&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主 题：[Chessnut Support] Business / Partnership - Chessnut Move New support request from Chessnut website: Name: David Mitchel Rios Bernal Email: david@popokani.mx Order Number: N/A Inquiry Type: Business / Partnership Product: Chessnut Move Description: Hello Chessnut Team, My name is David Rios and I am currently evaluating the market for smart chess products in Mexico. I recently discovered the Chessnut Move and became very interested in the product and its potential in the Mexican market. I have previous experience importing and distributing specialty products in Mexico and I am evaluating whether Chessnut products could fit within a future commercial project focused on smart chess technology. I would appreciate information regarding: * Distributor / reseller programs * Wholesale pricing * Minimum order quantities (MOQ) * Sample purchase options * Current distribution status in Mexico * Whether Mexico currently has an exclusive distributor Thank you for your time and I look forward to hearing from you. Best regards, David Mitchel Rios Bernal david@popokani.mx Video Link: N/A --- Submitted via Chessnut Contact Form",
