the country until recently, so I’m just catching up on everything now. For now, here is the board information: Model number: CM100 Serial number: CMB6300533 Charging port model number: CHGCM1 In terms of the pieces affected, it is a little difficult to identify each specific piece, but I would say at least half of the pieces seem to be affected. I also wanted to mention that we have already begun putting out some basic introduction videos about the Chessnut Move unit, and we also incorporated it into our May 24th chess event, which was a huge success. Many parents showed a lot of interest in the unit, and it was definitely something that caught people’s attention. That said, I have held off on creating a full review of the Chessnut Move for the time being until we can hopefully resolve the issue. I’m very grateful that Chessnut provided the unit, and there are many wonderful features that I would be excited to highlight properly. At the same time, I want to make sure that any review I share is fair, honest, and genuinely useful for the families and chess players who follow us. I think it is important that I speak accurately about the full experience, including both the strengths of the unit and any practical notes around setup, troubleshooting, or things that may still need to be addressed. Also, for the videos we have shared so far, we did tag Chessnut. I just wanted to ask whether you received our collaboration requests for those videos. Going forward, when we feature the Chessnut Move unit, do you prefer that we simply tag Chessnut, or would you prefer that we send collaboration requests and post them as collab videos when appropriate? I’ll do my best to send the short video once I’m able to properly test and record the issue. Thank you again for your help, and sorry again for the delayed response. Arash Shahi &quot;Mr. S&quot; Executive Director CHESS WITH MR. S INC. www.chesswithmrs.com Mobile: 416.456.1599 info@chesswithmrs.com shahiarash.s@gmail.com On Wed, May 27, 2026 at 5:04 AM Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Hi Arash, Sorry for the delayed response. Could you please share your board&#39;s serial number, a short video of the issue, and how many pieces are affected? I will have my colleague Gwen get back to you shortly. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Arash Shahi &lt; info@chesswithmrs.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年5月23日(周六) 07:40 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主 题：Re: Collaboration Opportunity – Chessnut Move Feature Hi Stella, I hope you’re doing very well. First and foremost, thank you once again to you and the Chessnut team for the incredibly generous gift of the Chessnut Move unit. I truly appreciate it. As you know, we have our Spring Checkmate Festival this Sunday, May 24th, with 120 registered chess players plus their families attending, and we’ll be proudly showcasing the Chessnut Move unit as part of the event experience. I also plan to begin creating some content sharing my experience with the product and my broader thoughts on it, as I genuinely think the technology is incredibly impressive. Quite honestly, if someone didn’t know better, it almost feels magical seeing it in action. That said, I wanted to reach out because I seem to be experiencing an issue that appears to be similar to something other Chessnut Move owners have reported. After fully charging the board and pieces, when everything is powered down completely (board turned off, app closed, and everything fully disconnected), some of the pieces continue to twitch or make tiny unintended movements while resting on the board. I did a little digging online and it seems others may have encountered similar behaviour, so I wanted to ask whether this is a known issue and whether there’s a recommended fix, firmware update, reset procedure, or best practice to resolve it. This likely won’t impact our tournament demo on Sunday, so there’s no emergency—but I’d really like to understand what’s happening. As I begin sharing my thoughts on the product and potentially recommending it to our broader chess community of students, families, and chess enthusiasts, I’d love to be able to confidently explain whether this behaviour is expected, avoidable, or fixable. Because truthfully, I think this is a remarkable product with real appeal for chess-loving families and adult enthusiasts alike. If helpful, I’d also be happy to send along a short video of the twitching behaviour. Thanks again for all of your kindness and support—I’d really appreciate any guidance from you or your technical team. Warmly, Arash Shahi &quot;Mr. S&quot; Executive Director CHESS WITH MR. S INC. www.chesswithmrs.com Mobile: 416.456.1599 info@chesswithmrs.com shahiarash.s@gmail.com On Fri, May 8, 2026 at 3:42 AM Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; wrote: Hi Arash, That should be it. The tracking number has been updated: 1ZB87K330420800754. Carrier: UPS. You should receive it soon. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Arash Shahi &lt; info@chesswithmrs.com &gt; 发送时间：2026年4月30日(周四) 23:44 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; 主 题：Re: Collaboration Opportunity – Chessnut Move Feature Hi Stella, I hope you’re doing well, and my apologies for the slow response. We’re very excited to get started with this collaboration. I’ve gone ahead and completed the Uppromote application using the link you provided, and I’m looking forward to receiving the promotion code. We’re planning to share the code with all of our students’ families, especially those attending our upcoming tournament, and we’ll also be featuring the Chessnut Move at a demo station during the event. It should be a great opportunity for families to experience it firsthand. Thanks again, and please let me know if there’s anything further needed on m