      "body": "Hi Stella, Thank you so much! Everything looks great on our end! We updated our payout details as well. Thanks again! Warmest regards, Tammy > On Jun 25, 2026, at 2:57 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: > > Hi Tammy, > > Thanks for confirming! I’ve already adjusted your commission to 10% — please check on your end. > > > Also, please make sure to fill in your payout details. Chessnut processes payments at the beginning of each month for the previous month’s commissions. > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > > > ------------------------------------------------------------------ > 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships > 发送时间：2026年6月25日(周四) 15:39 > 收件人：Stella Zhuang > 主 题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry > > Hi Stella, > > Thank you so much! We have registered under the email address: partner@blackmediapresents.com > > Thanks again and we are looking forward to what’s to come! > > Warmest regards, > Tammy > > > On Jun 24, 2026, at 1:03 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: > > Hi Tammy, > > Thank you for the clarification — I really appreciate it. And yes, 10% works perfectly for us. > To get started, please go ahead and register through the link I shared earlier. Once you’ve registered, just send me the email address you used, and I’ll adjust your commission to 10% on our end. > As for the sponsored live stream series — we’re not looking to explore that at this stage, but we’re excited to move forward with the studio integration and affiliate collaboration. > Let me know once you’ve registered! > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > > ------------------------------------------------------------------ > 发件人：Black Media Partnerships > 发送时间：2026年6月24日(周三) 06:44 > 收件人：Stella Zhuang > 主 题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry > > Hi Stella, > > Thank you so much for taking the time to share your concerns. Looking back at how I laid out our options, I can see how it may have read as tying the studio access to a paid package. That was not my intention at all, and I am sorry for the confusion. I want to clear things up because we are absolutely still on the same page as where we started. > > The studio integration and product placement is very much our intention and always has been. The chess board is in the studio, we've been demonstrating it to Howie and our guests, and everyone who sees it in action is blown away. That organic exposure, as well as any press, TV coverage, interviews, or a guest trying it out, is still what we're doing. If any of that finds its way into press, TV, or social media naturally, that is exactly what we want to provide in exchange for you sending the boards. > > Regarding the flat fee and higher commission mention, that was specific to a separate format entirely: targeted, sales-focused social media videos designed to convert using our affiliate link. Those dedicated posts require a different level of creative investment and are built to drive direct sales, which is why the compensation structure looks different for that format. That said, we actually prefer the commission route over a flat fee, and we are fully on board with the 10%. None of this affects the studio integration, which remains exactly as we originally discussed. > > The one additional idea we wanted to put on the table, and only if you have budget for it in the future, is a sponsored live stream series. This would look like longer-form live chess streams on TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, etc., two to three times a month, with the possibility of bringing in celebrity guests to play. That would be a separate paid sponsorship conversation, and entirely optional. If it is not in the budget, no worries at all. It does not affect anything we already have in place; we just feel it could be incredible exposure and could really increase sales. > > We are so excited about this partnership and want it to feel as good on your end as it does on ours. Please let us know if you have any questions and also when we can get started with the SUNNYLOVE code and 10% commission! > > Thank you so much. > > Warmest regards, > Tammy > > On Jun 23, 2026, at 1:03 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: > > > Hi Tammy, > > I just want to make sure I understand correctly. In our earlier conversations, the idea was that Chessnut boards would be placed naturally in the studio — as part of the background in interviews, or as something that might come up organically if Howie or other guests noticed them. That’s the kind of exposure we were originally excited about. > Now it seems like we’re being offered paid social media content instead. That’s a very different direction from what we discussed earlier. > To be direct: paid content isn’t something we can consider. And on the commission side, our maximum is 10% — that’s the highest we offer. > We’d still love to explore the studio integration — having Chessnut boards appear naturally in the background of interviews or studio content, with the possibility of organic moments with Howie or other talent. That kind of authentic exposure is what we’d really like to focus on. > If that’s still possible, we’re happy to continue the conversation. If not, we completely understand — and we can leave it here. > Let us know your thoughts. > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > ------------------------------------------------------------------ > 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships > 发送时间：2026年6月17日(周三) 13:20 > 收件人：Stella Zhuang > 主 题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry > > Hi Stella, > > Thank you so much for your message. We are so excited about Chessnut and truly believe in what you have built. > > Before we finalize everything, we wanted to share how we typically structure our brand partnerships so we can find the right fit for both sides. We have two options depending on what works best for Chessnut: > > Option A: Performance-Based Partnership > > A 20% affiliate commission with no flat fee. This is our partnership track, where we are both fully invested in driving sales. You pay nothing upfront, and we are motivated to push the product through our social media channels because our earnings are tied directly to performance. > > Option B: Guaranteed Content Package > > A 5% affiliate commission plus a flat fee of $4,000 per dedicated short-form video. This option gives you guaranteed, high-quality content delivered to our combined audience of 1.9 million followers across Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, and YouTube, regardless of conversion. It also includes the organic celebrity and press exposure we have access to through Howie Mandel's studio, which is something truly unique to us. > > One additional benefit worth mentioning: through our access at Howie Mandel's studio, celebrity content opportunities come up organically. When they do, we will reach out with the details and give you the option to add it on as a dedicated piece of content. Two of the primary celebrity formats would be 1) when a celebrity engages with and responds to seeing Chessnut in action in real time, and 2) product gifting videos, where we demonstrate the board and gift a Chessnut to the celebrity on camera (this requires having a small stock on hand). The gifting format in particular tends to create warm, heartfelt moments that highlight the product naturally, and often results in the celebrity posting about it on their own channels at a later date, extending the reach of the content well beyond our own audience. These opportunities typically start at $10,000, and as a partner we would offer those to you at a reduced rate. > > Both options come with our full creative investment and the SUNNYLOVE affiliate code active and promoted across our content and community. > > We would love to hear which structure feels like the best fit on your end, and we are happy to talk through either option in more detail. > > Warmest regards, > Tammy > > On Jun 10, 2026, at 12:53 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: > > Hi Tammy, 