 > > Hi Stella, > > I wanted to check in and see if you had any questions or thoughts on everything we shared. We are very excited about the possibilities here and happy to chat through anything! > > Looking forward to hearing from you! > > Warmest regards, > Tammy > > On Apr 10, 2026, at 2:41 AM, BlackMedia Partnerships wrote: > > Hi Stella, > > Thank you so much for your thoughtful response. We are very excited about what's possible here! > > To best understand what's realistic and structure a partnership that truly suits Chessnut, we'd love to start by testing two units, one at Howie's studio and one at our sister studio, both of which have a steady flow of celebrity guests and filming sets. One of our top priorities would be getting Chessnut in front of Howie so he can personally experience it. This would also let us see how the boards look on our sets, how they integrate organically into the studio environment, and test the functionality with our full team. > > If this sounds good to you, we'd love your recommendation on the two models you feel would be most visually striking on camera and most impressive in person, the ones that would really create that wow-factor for celebrities and social media alike. You know your product better than anyone, and we want to make sure we would be showcasing Chessnut in the best possible light. > > From there, we can build out a realistic and well-rounded partnership plan together. > > Looking forward to hearing your thoughts! > > Warmest regards, > > Tammy Byerly > Strategic Partnerships > Black Media Co., LLC > https://linktr.ee/BlackMediaContact > > > On Apr 9, 2026, at 5:12 AM, Stella Zhuang wrote: > > Hi Tammy, > > Thanks again for the detailed introduction — really impressive network you've built. > > What caught our attention most is your access to Howie Mandel's ecosystem: > > The podcast (Howie Mandel Does Stuff) > > The LA studio with celebrity guests > > GGL and the celebrity gaming league > > If a partnership can tap into those — for example, product placement in the studio, a mention on the podcast, or Howie/Sunny naturally using Chessnut in content — that's where we see the real value. > > Could you help us understand what's realistic here, and what kind of partnership you had in mind? > > Looking forward to your thoughts. > > Best, > Stella > Business Development Manager | Chessnut > > > ------------------------------------------------------------------ > 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships > 发送时间：2026年4月8日(周三) 04:16 > 收件人：Stella Zhuang > 主 题：Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry > > Dear Stella, > > Vincent Lo gave me your email address so I could contact you about partnership opportunties with Chessnut. We’ve been following Chessnut's journey and think what you're building is brilliant and beautifully crafted. We really admire what you’re doing to revolutionize chess. I'm Tammy, and I work on Strategic Partnerships for Sunny and The Black Pack, the Official House Band & Gaming Team of Howie Mandel (of the hit shows America’s Got Talents and Deal or No Deal). We are also part of the Global Gaming League alongside T-Pain. We'd love to connect and explore what opportunities there might be to partner with Chessnut. > > We work out of Howie's studio in Los Angeles, which is an incredible playground of music, cutting-edge technology, art, and entertainment, with frequent high-profile celebrity guests. Within the studio, we live stream, film TV shows, music videos, and podcasts, including podcasts hosted by Howie Mandel, Billy Corgan of The Smashing Pumpkins, Jack Osbourne, Jillian Michaels, Billy Bush, and Holly Madison. We are part of Howie's podcast Howie Mandel Does Stuff, with guests like Sofia Vergara of Modern Family, Heidi Klum, Terry Crews, Simon Cowell, Tim Allen, Kris Jenner, Oliver Tree and many more. > > Some links to help you get to know us better: > > Global Gaming League (we are team “Howie Do It”): https://youtu.be/diBz3ZrWDpM > Michael Bublé with Sunny and The Black Pack: https://youtu.be/KdZpc87sQ7o > Richie Sambora of Bon Jovi with Sunny and The Black Pack: https://youtu.be/arei8ZOEdOw > Logic with Sunny and The Black Pack: https://youtu.be/XLai0lZHN5I > Gene Simmons of KISS with Sunny and The Black Pack: https://www.instagram.com/p/DE0PUYlyrqE/ > Rob Lowe with Sunny and The Black Pack: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DMIRzDlOzTb/ > Arsenio Hall with Sunny and The Black Pack: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DAGrx6tvFBk/ > Jason Alexander of Seinfeld bass gift: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DBHF7VgvqE4/ > Skechers Holiday TV Ad starred in and wrote and recorded music: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DRxjIs7Eth8/ > > We have over 1.8 million followers across platforms and influential followers like Howie Mandel, Michael Bublé, David Arquette, Arsenio Hall, Danny Trejo, Tom Green, Paula Abdul, Adrian Grenier, Zedd, The Sound of Music, Sal Vulcano, Kenny Loggins, Kurt Sutter, Robert and Dean DeLeo of Stone Temple Pilots, Dick Van Dyke, Gary Busey, Ray J, Kevin Nealon of Saturday Night Live and many others. > > Instagram (399K Followers): https://www.instagram.com/blackmediapresents > Facebook (811K Followers): https://www.facebook.com/sunnyandtheblackpack > TikTok (591K Followers): https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmediapresents > YouTube (64K Subscribers): https://www.youtube.com/blackmediapresents > > Here are links to collaborations, along with our social channels: > https://linktr.ee/BlackMediaContact > > We'd love to explore ways we can bring Chessnut to even more people through content, studio integration, social media, and celebrity moments. Please let us know if you have any ideas or if you’d like to schedule a Google Meet so we can discuss further. > > Thank you so much! > > Warmest regards, > > Tammy Byerly > Strategic Partnerships > Black Media Co., LLC > https://linktr.ee/BlackMediaContact > > > > > > > > --Apple-Mail=_69245FC9-1272-4B4A-9CDB-349CF0C95CB3 Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8 Hi Stella, Thank you so much! Everything looks great on our end! We updated our payout details as well. Thanks again! Warmest regards, Tammy On Jun 25, 2026, at 2:57 AM, Stella Zhuang &lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; wrote: Hi Tammy, Thanks for confirming! I’ve already adjusted your commission to 10% — please check on your end. &lt;temp4cj.png&gt; Also, please make sure to fill in your payout details. Chessnut processes payments at the beginning of each month for the previous month’s commissions. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：BlackMedia Partnerships &lt;partner@blackmediapresents.com&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月25日(周四) 15:39 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主 题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry Hi Stella, Thank you so much! We have registered under the email address: partner@blackmediapresents.com &nbsp; Thanks again and we are looking forward to what’s to come! Warmest regards, Tammy On Jun 24, 2026, at 1:03 AM, Stella Zhuang &lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; wrote: Hi Tammy, Thank you for the clarification — I really appreciate it. And yes, 10% works perfectly for us. To get started, please go ahead and register through the link I shared earlier. Once you’ve registered, just send me the email address you used, and I’ll adjust your commission to 10% on our end. As for the sponsored live stream series — we’re not looking to explore that at this stage, but we’re excited to move forward with the studio integration and affiliate collaboration. Let me know once you’ve registered! Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：Black Media Partnerships &lt;partner@blackmediapresents.com&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月24日(周三) 06:44 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主 题：Re: Chessnut // BlackMediaPresents - Partnership Inquiry Hi Stella, Thank you so much for taking the time to share your concerns. Looking back at how I laid out our options, I can see how it may have read as tying the studio access to a paid package. That was not my intention at all, and I am sorry for the confusion. I want to clear things up because we are absolutely still on the same page as where we started. The studio integration and product placement is very much our intention and always has been. The chess board is in the studio, we've been demonstrating it to Howie and our guests, and everyone who sees it in action is blown away. That organic exposure, as well as any press, TV coverage, interviews, or a guest trying it out, is still what we're doing. If any of that finds its way into press, TV, or social media naturally, that is exactly what we want to provide in exchange for you sending the boards. Regarding the flat fee and higher commission mention, that was specific to a separate format entirely: targeted, sales-focused social media videos designed to convert using our affiliate link. Those dedicated posts require a different level of creative investment and are built to drive direct sales, which is why the compensation structure looks different for that format. That said, we actually prefer the commission route over a flat fee, and we are fully on board with the 10%. None of this affects the studio integration, which remains exactly as we originally discussed. The one additional idea we wanted to put on the table, and only if you have budget for it in the future, is a sponsored live stream series. This would look like longer-form live chess streams on TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, etc., two to three times a month, with the possibility of bringing in celebrity guests to play. That would be a separate paid sponsorship conversation, and entirely optional. If it is not in the budget, no worries at all. It does not affect anything we already have in place; we just feel it could be incredible exposure and could really increase