 have a few questions: - Are you part of Marianczello’s team, or an independent organizer working with him? - Could you clarify the structure of the 10-tournament cycle? Is it 10 separate events with their own winners, or a points-based series leading to one overall champion? - Roughly how many players have registered so far? - You mentioned that 3 boards would help ‘create massive buzz across the 10-tournament cycle’ — could you clarify what the exposure channels look like? Are there social media promotions, media coverage, or other content formats? We’d also be open to co-creating content together. This will help us get a clearer picture and move forward more confidently. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl &lt;krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月25日(周四) 15:05 收件人：&#34;stella.zhuang&#34;&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主 题：Partnership X Marianczello Decade Series Dear Stella, Thank you for the quick response! I am very excited about your interest in collaborating. To give you more details about the event: I am the official organizer of the Marianczello Decade Series —a prestigious cycle of 10 tournaments celebrating Marianczello&#39;s 10th anniversary of chess content creation. He is the biggest chess YouTuber in Poland, with a community of over 150,000 subscribers and 50,000 members in our Chess.com Chess.com club. Initially, I mentioned a single board, but after finalizing the tournament structure, we would love to upgrade this to a partnership involving 3 Chessnut boards . This will allow us to create a massive buzz and maximize the marketing value for Chessnut across the entire 10-tournament cycle: 1st Board: The ultimate Grand Prix prize for the overall winner of the Decade Series. 2nd Board: The prize for the runner-up (2nd place) in the final standings. 3rd Board: A grand raffle prize for all participants. At the end of the series, we will host a big giveaway drawing from everyone who played, which is the perfect tool to keep everyday amateur players highly engaged and active from the first to the very last tournament. In exchange for these 3 boards, we will provide an extensive promotional campaign: Club Homepage Banner: A prominent Chessnut banner on our main Chess.com Chess.com club page for the entire duration of the series. Dedicated Articles &amp; Newsletters: Official tournament announcements on Chess.com Chess.com with direct links to your store, sent to our 50,000 club members. YouTube Video Integration: Marianczello will personally provide dedicated sponsor shoutouts, mention your brand in his videos, and include direct links in the descriptions of his tournament coverage videos on YouTube. This setup ensures high, long-term player engagement and puts Chessnut products directly in front of thousands of passionate Polish chess players for months. Please let me know if this expanded package works for you! Best regards, Krzysztof Dettlaff Tournament Organizer www.chess.com https://www.chess.com/events/info/marianczello-decade-series m.youtube.com https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=41iJsK6L7mI 1:20 Last video and Youtuber talk about tournament and sponsors :) --2CVNLIHPYBHVIPLQHCNNBnhgwp Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable Content-Type: text/html; charset=UTF-8 Hi Stella, Thanks for your message and the great ideas! Showing the physical Chessnut boards in the video is definitely a smart move to boost engagement. To answer your questions: Other Sponsors: Yes, we have other brand partners on board, all strictly related to chess. They are Chess.com , Caissa, szachownica3d.pl , Exclusive Sport, Marianczello Sklep, and Węgiel Chess. Prize Distribution: We plan to award the 3 Chessnut boards at the very end of the 10-tournament series. Two boards will go directly to the TOP 2 players in the final Grand Prix standings. The third board will be used for a giveaway raffle—anyone who participates in more than 50% of the tournaments (at least 6 out of 10) will be entered for a chance to win it. Presentation: In the official regulations and the prize section, your products will be clearly highlighted with the exact product name and your company logo, listed alongside the other sponsors. Regarding Content &amp; Next Steps: To give you some context, I am managing the official Chess.com club and the tournament logistics, while Maciej (Marianczello) is the creator and the face of the channel. To sum up from my end: I will ensure that your brand is highly visible to all players on Chess.com throughout these few months of the series. As for the YouTube content, including the video timeline, it is open for discussion. I can certainly propose to Maciej that he records a dedicated Reel/Short featuring your products. To move forward, could you please send me a final summary of your expectations from Chessnut's side? Once I have your specific proposal, I will review it with Maciej and get back to you with our confirmation. Looking forward to collaborating with you! Best regards, Krzysztof Dettlaff Event Organizator and Admin Marianczello Club Dnia 26 czerwca 2026 08:32 Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; napisał(a): Hi Krzysztof, Thanks for the detailed response — this is very helpful. On co-created content: I was thinking we could tag each other when posting Shorts or Reels, so Chessnut’s 60K followers can also discover the tournament. I think that could be a nice boost for visibility on your side too. Also, it might be helpful to feature the prize boards briefly in Marianczello’s video — showing the actual products could make them more appealing to players. The Move is quite popular right now, so that could generate some extra interest. Before we confirm the prize commitment, I have a couple of questions: - Are there other brand sponsors involved in the series besides Chessnut? If so, could you share who they are? - How will the 3 Chessnut boards be used across the 10 tournaments? Will they be awarded at the final Grand Prix standings, or distributed across individual events? - If there are other sponsors, will the Chessnut boards be presented as standalone prizes, or grouped together with other sponsor items? Also, could you confirm the timeline for Marianczello’s YouTube videos and mentions? Looking forward to your reply! Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl &lt;krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月25日(周四) 18:36 收件人：Stella Zhuang&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主 题：Odp: 回复：Partnership X Marianczello Decade Series Hi Stella, I am the lead organizer and creator of this event, as well as the administrator of the MARIANCZELLO Club on Chess.com . Marianczello and I are close friends; he was actually my very first chess coach. This entire cycle is being organized to celebrate his 10th anniversary as a content creator. To answer your questions directly: Role &amp; Structure: I operate independently but with Marianczello's full backing. This is a non-profit project driven entirely by my passion to popularize chess. There are no entry fees, and I am not making any profit from it. Tournament Format: It is a hybrid Grand Prix system consisting of 10 monthly editions . In each standalone edition, the top 3 players win prizes, and additional sponsor items are raffled among all participants. Concurrently, the top 30 players from each edition earn points toward a general Grand Prix standing. The biggest guaranteed prizes are reserved for the overall Top 6, alongside a separate raffle pool for active club members. Timeline: We kick off this Sunday, June 28 . Each subsequent edition will take place on the last Sunday of every month, concluding with the grand finale in March 2027 . Player Turnout &amp; Registration: The event is officially hosted on the Chess.com Events platform. Because of how the platform works, offi