      "id": "18205d6de6e7f1532797",
      "threadId": "odp: 回复：partnership x marianczello decade series",
      "name": "krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl",
      "email": "krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl",
      "subject": "Odp: 回复：Partnership X Marianczello Decade Series",
      "summary": "Hi Stella, I am the lead organizer and creator of this event, as well as the administrator of the MARIANCZELLO Club on Chess.com Chess.com . Marianczello and I ",
      "body": "Hi Stella, I am the lead organizer and creator of this event, as well as the administrator of the MARIANCZELLO Club on Chess.com Chess.com . Marianczello and I are close friends; he was actually my very first chess coach. This entire cycle is being organized to celebrate his 10th anniversary as a content creator. To answer your questions directly: Role &amp; Structure: I operate independently but with Marianczello&#39;s full backing. This is a non-profit project driven entirely by my passion to popularize chess. There are no entry fees, and I am not making any profit from it. Tournament Format: It is a hybrid Grand Prix system consisting of 10 monthly editions . In each standalone edition, the top 3 players win prizes, and additional sponsor items are raffled among all participants. Concurrently, the top 30 players from each edition earn points toward a general Grand Prix standing. The biggest guaranteed prizes are reserved for the overall Top 6, alongside a separate raffle pool for active club members. Timeline: We kick off this Sunday, June 28 . Each subsequent edition will take place on the last Sunday of every month, concluding with the grand finale in March 2027 . Player Turnout &amp; Registration: The event is officially hosted on the Chess.com Chess.com Events platform. Because of how the platform works, official player registration opens exactly one hour before the tournament starts. However, based on our club&#39;s active community size, we are expecting a very strong turnout. Exposure &amp; Marketing: We have fantastic channels lined up! Chess.com Chess.com Polska has already published information about our tournament and will promote it again right before the launch. Additionally, Marianczello will be live-streaming parts of the tournament cycle (schedule permitting). We are also planning to include dedicated sponsor mentions and product placements directly inside Marianczello’s upcoming YouTube videos. Regarding your mention of co-creating content, could you please provide more details on what exactly you have in mind? Once I have more specifics, I will consult directly with Marianczello to see what formats we can best integrate into his channel. Please let me know if this structure aligns with Chessnut&#39;s goals, and we can discuss how to move forward! Best regards, Krzysztof Lead Organizer | MARIANCZELLO Club Dnia 25 czerwca 2026 12:07 Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; napisał(a): Hi Krzysztof, Thanks for the detailed proposal — it sounds like a well-structured event with strong community backing. Before we move forward, I have a few questions: - Are you part of Marianczello’s team, or an independent organizer working with him? - Could you clarify the structure of the 10-tournament cycle? Is it 10 separate events with their own winners, or a points-based series leading to one overall champion? - Roughly how many players have registered so far? - You mentioned that 3 boards would help ‘create massive buzz across the 10-tournament cycle’ — could you clarify what the exposure channels look like? Are there social media promotions, media coverage, or other content formats? We’d also be open to co-creating content together. This will help us get a clearer picture and move forward more confidently. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl &lt;krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月25日(周四) 15:05 收件人：&#34;stella.zhuang&#34;&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主 题：Partnership X Marianczello Decade Series Dear Stella, Thank you for the quick response! I am very excited about your interest in collaborating. To give you more details about the event: I am the official organizer of the Marianczello Decade Series —a prestigious cycle of 10 tournaments celebrating Marianczello&#39;s 10th anniversary of chess content creation. He is the biggest chess YouTuber in Poland, with a community of over 150,000 subscribers and 50,000 members in our Chess.com Chess.com club. Initially, I mentioned a single board, but after finalizing the tournament structure, we would love to upgrade this to a partnership involving 3 Chessnut boards . This will allow us to create a massive buzz and maximize the marketing value for Chessnut across the entire 10-tournament cycle: 1st Board: The ultimate Grand Prix prize for the overall winner of the Decade Series. 2nd Board: The prize for the runner-up (2nd place) in the final standings. 3rd Board: A grand raffle prize for all participants. At the end of the series, we will host a big giveaway drawing from everyone who played, which is the perfect tool to keep everyday amateur players highly engaged and active from the first to the very last tournament. In exchange for these 3 boards, we will provide an extensive promotional campaign: Club Homepage Banner: A prominent Chessnut banner on our main Chess.com Chess.com club page for the entire duration of the series. Dedicated Articles &amp; Newsletters: Official tournament announcements on Chess.com Chess.com with direct links to your store, sent to our 50,000 club members. YouTube Video Integration: Marianczello will personally provide dedicated sponsor shoutouts, mention your brand in his videos, and include direct links in the descriptions of his tournament coverage videos on YouTube. This setup ensures high, long-term player engagement and puts Chessnut products directly in front of thousands of passionate Polish chess players for months. Please let me know if this expanded package works for you! Best regards, Krzysztof Dettlaff Tournament Organizer www.chess.com https://www.chess.com/events/info/marianczello-decade-series m.youtube.com https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=41iJsK6L7mI 1:20 Last video and Youtuber talk about tournament and sponsors :) --2NILPHIKAJWMPIXRKELKSnhgwp Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable Content-Type: text/html; charset=UTF-8 Hi Stella, I am the lead organizer and creator of this event, as well as the administrator of the MARIANCZELLO Club on Chess.com . Marianczello and I are close friends; he was actually my very first chess coach. This entire cycle is being organized to celebrate his 10th anniversary as a content creator. To answer your questions directly: Role &amp; Structure: I operate independently but with Marianczello's full backing. This is a non-profit project driven entirely by my passion to popularize chess. There are no entry fees, and I am not making any profit from it. Tournament Format: It is a hybrid Grand Prix system consisting of 10 monthly editions . In each standalone edition, the top 3 players win prizes, and additional sponsor items are raffled among all participants. Concurrently, the top 30 players from each edition earn points toward a general Grand Prix standing. The biggest guaranteed prizes are reserved for the overall Top 6, alongside a separate raffle pool for active club members. Timeline: We kick off this Sunday, June 28 . Each subsequent edition will take place on the last Sunday of every month, concluding with the grand finale in March 2027 . Player Turnout &amp; Registration: The event is officially hosted on the Chess.com Events platform. Because of how the platform works, official player registration opens exactly one hour before the tournament starts. However, based on our club's active community size, we are expecting a very strong turnout. Exposure &amp; Marketing: We have fantastic channels lined up! Chess.com Polska has already published information about our tournament and will promote it again right before the launch. Additionally, Marianczello will be live-streaming parts of the tournament cycle (schedule permitting). We are also planning to include dedicated sponsor mentions and product placements directly inside Marianczello’s upcoming YouTube videos. Regarding your mention of co-creating content, could you please provide more details on what exactly you have in mind? Once I have more specifics, I will consult directly with Marianczello to see what formats we can best integrate into his channel. Please let me know if this structure aligns with Chessnut's goals, and we can discuss how to move forward! Best regards, Krzysztof Lead Organizer | MARIANCZELLO Club Dnia 25 czerwca 2026 12:07 Stella Zhuang &lt; stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com &gt; napisał(a): Hi Krzysztof, Thanks for the detailed proposal — it sounds like a well-structured event with strong community backing. Before we move forward, I have a few questions: - Are you part of Marianczello’s team, or an independent organizer working with him? - Could you clarify the structure of the 10-tournament cycle? Is it 10 separate events with their own winners, or a points-based series leading to one overall champion? - Roughly how many players have registered so far? - You mentioned that 3 boards would help ‘create massive buzz across the 10-tournament cycle’ — could you clarify what the exposure channels look like? Are there social media promotions, media coverage, or other content formats? We’d also be open to co-creating content together. This will help us get a clearer picture and move forward more confidently. Best, Stella Business Development Manager | Chessnut ------------------------------------------------------------------ 发件人：krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl &lt;krzysiekdettlaff@wp.pl&gt; 发送时间：2026年6月25日(周四) 15:05 收件人：\"stella.zhuang\"&lt;stella.zhuang@chessnutech.com&gt; 主 题：Partnership X Marianczello Decade Series Dear Stella, Thank you for the quick response! I am very excited about your interest in collaborating. To give you more details about the event: I am the official organizer of the Marianczello Decade Series —a prestigious cycle of 10 tournaments celebrating Marianczello's 10th anniversary of chess content creation. He is the biggest chess YouTuber in Poland, with a community of over 150,000 subscribers and 50,000 members in our Chess.com club. Initially, I mentioned 